hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12706","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, concerning a man who borrowed goods, then married a woman with them as dower, he said: The man takes back his goods, and their right is upon the one who deceived them."
"12707","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said to me: When a woman marries a man knowing him only as free, then slavery catches up with him, she is given the choice; if she wishes she stays with him, and if she wishes she leaves."
"12708","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If she proceeded while his slavery had been impugned to her, she has no choice afterwards. And Amr said: She has the choice, unless she was certain."
"12709","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who married a free woman, deceiving her about himself, and she did not know until he consummated with her, he said: She is given the choice; if she wishes she leaves him, and if she wishes she stays with him, and she has the dower of her equals for what he made lawful of her by deceiving her."
"12710","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that a slave boy married a woman, deceiving her about himself, and drove to her five young camels, then they disputed him to Uthman, so he annulled the marriage, gave her two young camels, and returned three to Abu Musa."
"12711","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to him: A slave married a free woman, deceiving her about himself, claiming he is free, and drove to her wealth belonging to his master. He said: Whatever of his wealth is found intact is taken, and what she consumed, there is nothing upon her for it. If the wealth belonged to the slave, it is hers. And I say, I and Ubayd Allah ibn Yazid: My wealth and my slave's wealth are the same; he takes it from her, and she shall have the like of the dower of her women."
"12712","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Layla said to me, from their jurists: The dower his slave boy gave her belongs to the master of the slave; he takes it from her. She hastened before knowing."
"12713","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed me, from Amir al-Shabi, or Abd Allah ibn Qays: There was a slave boy of Abu Musa, a shepherd, who deceived a free woman and married her without the permission of Abu Musa, giving her as dower five camels of Abu Musa's camels. So Uthman gave her two camels and returned three camels to him. She was a freedwoman of Abu Jafdah, and it was reported that the slave boy of Abu Musa had prospered."
"12714","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: It is not lawful for a freeman to marry a slave woman today while he can find a free woman with her dower. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus from his father, the same. He said: I said: But he fears fornication? He said: I do not know it to be lawful for him."
"12715","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: If he fears hardship for himself, let him marry her."
"12716","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ata saying: If he fears he will commit indecency with her, there is no harm in marrying her."
"12717","From al-Thawri, from one of his companions, he said: The freeman does not marry the slave woman unless he fears for himself. And Ibrahim mentioned it."
"12718","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: It is not lawful for a freeman to marry a slave woman while he can afford a free woman. From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, the same as the saying of Tawus."
"12719","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: Whoever finds the dower of a free woman shall not marry a slave woman."
"12720","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: The freeman does not marry the slave woman unless he fears for himself and cannot afford the free woman."
"12721","From Hushaym, from Mansur, from Zadham, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: They disliked the marriage of the slave woman in this time. They said: Marriage to them was permitted only when the free woman's maintenance was burdensome."
"12722","From a man, from Imran ibn Hudayr, from al-Nazzal, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When a man owns three hundred dirhams, Hajj becomes obligatory upon him, and slave women become unlawful for him."
"12723","From Ibn Saman, that he heard Mujahid saying concerning His saying: That is a lightening from your Lord and a mercy, he says: Concerning the marriage of slave women, he says: There is no harm in it."
"12724","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Mujahid, concerning a man marrying a slave woman, he said: It is among what was made ample for this ummah: the marriage of the slave woman and the Christian woman, even if he is wealthy. And Sufyan holds by it; he says: There is no harm in marrying the slave woman."
"12725","Then he mentioned the hadith of Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal, from Abbad ibn Abd Allah, from Ali, he said: When the free woman is married over the slave woman, the free woman has two days and the slave woman one day. That is because I asked him about marrying the slave woman, so he narrated to me this hadith of Ali, and said: I saw no harm in it."
"12726","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: It used to be said: The slave woman is not married over the free woman except by her consent. If they are gathered under him, the free woman has two-thirds of the maintenance, and the slave woman one-third."
"12727","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The slave woman is not married over the free woman, but the free woman is married over the slave woman."
"12728","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad ibn Abd Allah, he said: Ali said: When the free woman is married over the slave woman, the free woman has two days and the slave woman one day."
"12729","Ibn Jurayj informed us, and al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The free woman is married over the slave woman. He said: And the slave woman is not married over the free woman. If the free woman is pleased, she has two-thirds of the turn, and the slave woman one-third."
"12730","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib, they said: The slave woman is not married over the free woman, but the free woman is married over the slave woman. The free woman is apportioned two days and the slave woman one day, and maintenance likewise."
"12731","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, and from Dawud, from Ibn al-Musayyib, they said: If he marries the free woman over the slave woman, the free woman has two days and the slave woman one day."
"12732","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: If he marries the slave woman over the free woman, the free woman is given the choice; if she wishes to remain with him, she has twice what the slave woman has of turn and maintenance, and if she wishes they are separated from the slave woman."
"12733","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: There is no harm in marrying the free woman over the slave woman, but the slave woman is not married over the free woman. If he marries a slave woman over a free woman, he is separated from the slave woman and punished. If he marries a free woman over a slave woman while she knew there is a slave woman under him, she has twice what the slave woman has of turn and maintenance. If she was married without knowing there is a slave woman under him, she is given the choice; if she wishes she leaves him, and if she wishes she stays with him."
"12734","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me concerning the free woman married over the slave woman, that the Sunnah concerning her which the freeman acts upon is that the freeman does not marry a slave woman while he can afford a free woman. If he cannot afford, he is left to marry the slave woman. If he marries a free woman over her, he is left to that, if the free woman knew there is a slave woman under him. If she did not know, the free woman is given the choice between leaving him and staying with him, upon twice what the slave woman has of turn and maintenance. If he marries a slave woman over her, she is taken away and he is punished."
"12735","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he used to say: The slave woman and the free woman are not gathered in marriage under one man. Tawus said: And that you refrain from marrying the slave woman is better for you."
"12736","From al-Thawri, and Ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: As for marrying the slave woman over the free woman, it is like pork: he is compelled to it, then becomes free of need for it. He said: And there is no harm in the slave marrying the slave woman over the free woman."
"12737","From Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marrying the slave woman over the free woman."
"12738","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told from Said ibn Jubayr, saying: I do not see the marriage of the slave woman for the freeman as warding off fornication except a little. And from Abu Hurayrah the same."
"12739","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marrying the slave woman over the free woman."
"12740","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The marriage of the free woman over the slave woman is the divorce of the slave woman."
"12741","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When the slave marries the free woman, he has freed half of himself, and when the freeman marries the slave woman, he has enslaved half of himself. From Ibn Jurayj, he mentioned it from Umar the same."
"12742","From Mamar, from a man, from Ikrimah, that Luqman said: Do not marry the slave woman of another, lest you bequeath your children long grief."
"12743","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said concerning an owned Christian woman: The Muslim should not marry her. Have you not heard Allah saying: Of your believing slave women?"
"12744","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed Safiyyah, then made her freedom her dower. Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that, making her freedom her dower, but he did not mention that she was Safiyyah."
"12745","From al-Aslami, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, declared Safiyyah free of pregnancy by one menstruation."
"12746","From al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dower."
"12747","From Mamar, from a man of Hamdan, he said: A man from the people of Khurasan came to al-Shabi and said: With us there is a man who says: Whoever frees his slave woman then marries her is like one who rides his sacrificial camel. So Amir al-Shabi said: Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When a man disciplines the slave woman and disciplines her well, then frees her and marries her, he has two rewards. When a man of the People of the Book believes in his Book, then believes in our Book, he has two rewards. When the slave fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his master, he has two rewards. Then he said to him: Take it; I have given it to you without price. For journeys were undertaken to Madinah for what was easier than it."
"12748","From al-Thawri, from Salih, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has a slave girl, and disciplines her well and teaches her, teaching her well, then frees her and marries her, he has two rewards."
"12749","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: It reached us from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Three have their reward twice: a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his master, a man who frees his concubine then marries her, and a female convert of the People of the Book."
"12750","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, concerning the man who frees his slave girl then marries her, making her freedom her dower, he said: He has two rewards."
"12751","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: They used to dislike freeing her then marrying her, but saw no harm in making her freedom her dower. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said that is good."
"12752","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: There is no harm in a man freeing the slave woman, then marrying her and making her freedom her dower. Mamar said, and one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying the same."
"12753","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, he said: Juwayriyyah belonged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he freed her and made her dower the freeing of every captive of Banu al-Mustaliq."
"12754","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Juwayriyyah said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Your wives boast over me, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not marry you. So he said: Did I not make your dower great? Did I not free forty of your people?"
"12755","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When a man frees his slave woman, making her freedom her dower, then divorces her before consummating with her, there is no harm upon her."
"12756","From Ibn Jurayj, he says: If he divorces her, she strives to pay him half her value. And it is in the saying of whoever holds the saying of Ata."
"12757","From al-Thawri, he said: When a man divorces his wife, having made her freedom her dower, she strives to pay him half her value if he divorces her before consummating with her. This is in the saying of whoever says: Her freedom is her dower. And in the saying of whoever says: Making her freedom her dower is not a marriage, if he divorces her before consummating with her, she strives to pay her full value."
"12758","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Kanud, he said: Ibn Masud said: The like of one who frees his concubine then marries her is like one who gifts a sacrificial camel then rides it."
"12759","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said, concerning the man who frees the slave woman then marries her, he said: He gives her a dower besides her freedom."
"12760","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When a man frees her then marries her, let him name something by which he makes her lawful to him."
"12761","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: It does not harm a man if he does not call witnesses to the marriage of his male slave to his female slave, nor to the separation between them."
"12762","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik, from Umayr, from al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, that he wanted to marry a woman to whom he was a closer guardian than the one who was to marry her off to him, so he instructed another man, more distant than himself, and that man married her to him. Sufyan said: And the umm walad is in the same position if he frees her and then wants to marry her."
"12763","From al-Thawri, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about a woman who owns a female slave: should she marry her off herself? He said: No, but let her instruct her guardian and let him marry her off. Al-Thawri said: A man calls witnesses when he marries his female slave to his male slave or to another."
"12764","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: There is no marriage except with four: a guardian, a suitor, and two witnesses."
"12765","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: Witnesses distinguish fornication from marriage."
"12766","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If they publicize that, it suffices."
"12767","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the people: How many wives may a slave marry? They agreed that he should not exceed two."
"12768","From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri, both said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed us, from his father, that Ali said: A slave marries two."
"12769","From Ibn Uyayna, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Abu Talha, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: A slave marries two."
"12770","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the people: How many is it lawful for a slave to marry? Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: Two. Umar fell silent as if pleased with that and liking it. One of them said: He said: Umar said to him: You have agreed with what was in my mind."
"12771","From Ma'mar, he said: A slave marries two."
"12772","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: A slave marries four."
"12773","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May a slave marry four with his master's permission? It was as if he did not dislike that."
"12774","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, he said: A slave marries two. He said: And Mujahid said: He marries four."
"12775","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: Is there shighar regarding slave women? He said: No; she gets her dower."
"12776","From al-Thawri, he said: Shighar regarding slave women is like shighar regarding free women; if he makes a shighar arrangement for her, she gets a dower like hers."
"12777","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: Ibn Abbas said concerning a man who marries his female slave to his male slave without a dower: There is no harm in that."
"12778","From Ma'mar, he said: I was informed that it was disliked for a man to marry his male slave to his female slave without a dower, and it is recommended for him to name a dower."
"12779","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: They said concerning a female slave whom her master marries off, and her husband gives her a dower, paying part of the dower and leaving part, then her master frees her. They said: What remains of her dower owed by her husband belongs to her master, just as if he had hired her out to a man and her hire was due upon him, then he freed her, the hire would belong to her master."
"12780","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May a man marry his female slave to his male slave, or to a youth with him, without a dower? He said: No. Then I asked him after a while. He said: As for my own female slave, I marry her to my male slave without a dower. He said: Ibn Abbas used to say that."
"12781","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: It does not harm a man if he does not call witnesses to the marriage of his male slave to his female slave, and they are not to be separated."
"12782","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: Does a female slave married to a free man or to a slave get a parting gift? He said: No. I said: And a free woman married to a slave? He said: Nor she."
"12783","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: She has no parting gift."
"12784","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan saying: Every divorced woman gets a parting gift, and a female slave divorced by a male slave gets a parting gift if he divorces her."
"12785","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: And divorced women shall have provision."
"12786","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, concerning a free woman divorced by a slave while pregnant: Maintenance is upon the slave, but the nursing wage is not upon him. He said: And likewise a free man married to a female slave."
"12787","From al-Thawri: A pregnant divorced woman is maintained until she delivers her burden."
"12788","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached me that a free woman divorced by a slave while pregnant, when she delivers, he does not maintain her child because he does not inherit her, and he does not maintain her while pregnant except with his master's permission. And the female slave is likewise."
"12789","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata and others, concerning a female slave who comes to a people and tells them she is free, and one of them marries her, and she bears them children: their father ransoms the children."
"12790","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Musa mentioning that Umar ibn al-Khattab judged in such a case against their fathers: for every child of theirs among the slaves, valuation by span and cubit. I said to him: And his children were handsome? He said: The like of them in measure is not imposed."
"12791","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: Umar said to me: Learn from me three things: leadership is by consultation, and concerning the ransom of Arabs: in place of every slave, and concerning the son of a female slave: a slave. And Ibn Tawus concealed the third."
"12792","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, concerning a female slave whom a man marries thinking she is free, and she bears children. He said: Uthman judged concerning her children: in place of every male slave a slave, and in place of every slave girl two slave girls."
"12793","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab fixed the ransom of Arab captives at six shares. And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz fixed the ransom of Arab captives at four hundred dirhams per head. Ma'mar said: Then that was later abandoned regarding the people of Oman, and he said: They are free wherever you find them."
"12794","From al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Awn, from Ghadira al-Anbari, he said: We came to Umar ibn al-Khattab concerning women who were traded in the Jahiliyya, and he ordered that their children be valued against their fathers, and that they not be enslaved."
"12795","From Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash: Abu Husayn said, from al-Sha'bi, he said: When Umar was made caliph, he said: There is no ownership over an Arab, and we shall not take from anyone's hand anything over which he embraced Islam, but we shall value them at the full value."
"12796","From Ibn Uyayna, from Yahya al-Ashwai, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote that Umar ibn al-Khattab judged concerning the ransom of Arab captives: per head one hundred: four dirhams."
"12797","From Ibn Uyayna, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning Arab captives of the Jahiliyya that the ransom of a man is eight camels, and for a female ten. Ibn Uyayna said: al-Mujalid informed me, from al-Sha'bi, that that was complained of to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he made the ransom of a man four hundred dirhams."
"12798","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan saying: In place of every male slave a male slave, and in place of every slave girl a slave girl."
"12799","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning the ransom of Arab slaves from themselves: concerning a man taken captive in the Jahiliyya, eight camels; and concerning a child born of a female slave, two attendants, two attendants for each of them, male or female; and he judged concerning a Jahiliyya captive woman ten camels; and concerning her child by a slave, two attendants, whom the patrons of his mother ransom, and they are her paternal kin, theirs is her inheritance and his inheritance so long as his father is not freed; and he judged concerning captives of Islam six camels for a man, a woman, and a child. That is the ransom of Arabs."
"12800","From al-Thawri, concerning a female slave who deceives a free man about herself. Ali said: Upon the father is the value of the child; and if another than her had deceived him, the value would be upon the father, and he may claim from the one who deceived him. Al-Thawri said: And Ibrahim said: The value is reduced. He said: And Ibn Abi Layla said: They are valued when born, except that they are free. And al-Thawri said, and our saying is: They are valued when the judge judges concerning them."
"12801","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shu'ba, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked about a man who marries a female slave said to be free? He said: Her dower is upon the one who deceived him. He said: And Hammad said the like. He said: And al-Hakam said: If she bears a child, the redemption of the child is upon the father."
"12802","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, he said: A man married a female slave and she bore him a child; he wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz about that, and he wrote that he should ransom his children, whether the people of the Jahiliyya like it or dislike it."
"12803","From Ma'mar, from Sa'id, from Qatada, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: Her sale is her divorce."
"12804","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he said concerning a female slave sold while she has a husband: Her sale is her divorce."
"12805","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: Her sale is her divorce."
"12806","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Her sale is her divorce; but if the male slave is sold, she is not divorced thereby."
"12807","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: Her sale is her divorce, and whichever of the two is sold, that is her divorce; then if he marries her, he is not to separate."
"12808","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan, he said: Her sale is her divorce."
"12809","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ali said: He is her husband until he divorces her or dies."
"12810","From Ma'mar, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Shurahbil ibn al-Simt bought a slave girl and gifted her to Ali ibn Abi Talib - I think he said - Ali called her, and she said: I am occupied. He said: What occupies you? She said: I have a husband. He said: We have no need of something occupied, so return her to him."
"12811","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, that Sharahil ibn Murra sent a slave girl to Ali; Ali said to her: Are you free or occupied? She said: Occupied; I have a husband. So he returned her. Then Sharahil bought her marital rights for one thousand five hundred dirhams and sent her to Ali, and he accepted her."
"12812","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to her husband: You shall have so and so, but divorce her. He said: No."
"12813","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Kurayz gifted a slave girl from Basra to Uthman ibn Affan, and he was told she has a husband, so he returned her to him."
"12814","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada: They both disliked a female slave who has a husband, even if she is sold."
"12815","From Ma'mar, he said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: He was asked about a slave girl taken captive while she has a husband: is she lawful to her master? Al-Hasan said: Have you not seen the saying of al-Farazdaq: and one with a lover."
"12816","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, concerning a slave who pronounces zihar against his wife, a slave woman. He said: If he fasted a month, that would suffice him. Qatada said: And al-Hasan said: He fasts two months."
"12817","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, he said: He fasts two months unless his master permits him, then he frees a slave. From Uthman, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim the like."
"12818","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: He fasts two months; if they permit him to free a slave, it is allowed, and to feed if he pronounces zihar. Sufyan said: It is not allowed, because the wala would belong to another."
"12819","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Mujahid, concerning the expiation of a slave: A possessed slave owes only fasting and prayer."
"12820","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning the zihar of a slave: two months; he fasts two months."
"12821","From al-Thawri, concerning a slave who pronounces zihar or ila: It applies to him."
"12822","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: He has no ila apart from his master, and it is two months."
"12823","Ibn Jurayj said: It reached me that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The ila of a slave is two months."
"12824","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talha, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he said: The ila of a slave is two months."
"12825","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The ila of a slave from a female slave is four months."
"12826","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who pronounces zihar against his wife, a slave woman. He said: Half the fasting, and a slave has no zihar apart from his master."
"12827","From al-Thawri, he said: If a slave pronounces zihar or takes an oath of abstention, it applies to him."
"12828","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: The ila of a slave from a free woman is four months."
"12829","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata: concerning a slave who accuses his wife, a free woman, of adultery. He said: There is no li'an between them. He said: If a free man accuses his wife, a slave woman? He said: Nothing is upon him. He said: And if a slave accuses his wife, a slave woman, there is no mutual cursing between them; one who accuses a slave woman incurs nothing."
"12830","From al-Thawri, he said: Concerning a slave who accuses his wife, a slave woman. He said: There is no li'an between them; if a slave accuses his wife while she is free, he is flogged on her account and there is no li'an, and she remains his wife."
"12831","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a slave who accuses a free woman. He said: There is no li'an between them; he is flogged the hadd, and the child is attached to him."
"12832","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he said concerning a slave who accuses a free woman: There is no li'an between them."
"12833","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to him: If a man buys a female slave, may he look at her shanks, though she has menstruated, or at her belly? He said: Yes. Ata said: Ibn Umar used to place his hand between her breasts, look at her belly, look at her shanks, or order that."
"12834","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr or Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Ibn Umar, that he found traders gathered around a female slave; he uncovered part of her shank and placed his hand on her belly."
"12835","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar; and Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: When he wanted to buy a slave girl, after agreeing with them on a price, he placed his hand on her buttocks and looked at her shanks and her front, meaning her belly. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar the like."
"12836","From Ma'mar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar passed by people buying a slave girl; when they saw him while they were inspecting her, they stopped; Ibn Umar came to them, uncovered her shank, then pushed her chest and said: Buy. Ma'mar said: And Ibn Abi Najih informed me, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar placed his hand between her breasts, then shook her."
"12837","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, he said: I was with Ibn Umar in the market; he saw a slave girl being sold, uncovered her shank, struck her chest, and said: Buy - showing them that there is no harm in that."
"12838","From Ibn Uyayna, he said: And Ibn Abi Najih informed me, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar placed his hand between her breasts, then shook her."
"12839","From Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to uncover her back, belly, and shank, and place his hand on her buttocks."
"12840","From Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that he said: It is lawful for him to look at everything in her except her private part."
"12841","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: If a man is buying a female slave, he looks at all of her except the private part."
"12842","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: One whom I trust informed me, from one who heard Ali asking about a female slave being sold: may one look at her shank, buttocks, and belly? He said: There is no harm in that; she has no sanctity; she was only made to stand that we may bargain for her."
"12843","From al-Thawri, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from Ibrahim, from one of Abd Allah's companions, that he said concerning a female slave being sold: I do not care whether I touch her or the wall."
"12844","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Walid informed me that Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani informed him that Abu Bakr used to sell ummahat al-awlad during his rule, and Umar during half his rule; then Umar said: How can she be sold while her child is free? So he forbade her sale, until in Uthman's time they doubted, or embarked, concerning that."
"12845","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: We used to sell ummahat al-awlad while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive among us; we saw no harm in that."
"12846","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that it reached him that Ali wrote in his covenant: And I leave nineteen concubines; whichever of them has a child shall be valued against her child's share of inheritance from me, and whichever of them has no child is free. He said: So I asked Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn the elder: Is that in Ali's covenant? He said: Yes."
"12847","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ali wrote in his will: If something happens to me on this campaign - to proceed: my slave women whom I visit are nineteen slave girls; among them are mothers of children with their children, among them pregnant ones, and among them those with no child. I have decreed, if something happens to me on this campaign, that whichever of them is neither pregnant nor has a child is freed for the sake of Allah, no one having any claim on her; and whichever of them is pregnant or has a child shall be retained for her child, being from his share; if her child dies while she is alive, she is freed for the sake of Allah. This is what I have decreed concerning my nineteen slave women, and Allah is the One whose help is sought. Hayyaj ibn Abi Sufyan and Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi witnessed, and it was written in Jumada, year thirty-seven."
"12848","From Ibn Uyayna, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: A man of us died leaving an umm walad; al-Walid ibn Uqba wanted to sell her for his debt. So we came to Ibn Mas'ud and found him praying; we waited until he finished his prayer, and mentioned that to him. He said: If you must do it, place her in her child's share."
"12849","He said: Then two men came to him differing over a verse; one recited, and Abd Allah said: Well done; who taught you? He said: Abu Hakim al-Muzani taught me. Then he had the other recite, and said: Well done; who taught you? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab taught me. He said: Abd Allah wept until his tears wet the pebbles, then said: Recite as Umar taught you. Then he gestured around his house with his hand, then said: Umar was a strong fortress for Islam; people entered into it and did not leave. He said: When Umar died, the fortress was surrendered, and people leave it and do not enter it."
"12850","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shu'ba, from al-Hakam, from Utayba, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: I came to Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, I and a man, asking him about umm al-walad. He said: He was praying in the mosque with two men surrounding him on his right and left; when he finished his prayer, a man asked him about a verse of the Quran. He said: Who taught you? He said: Abu Hakim and Abu Amra taught me. And he said to the other: Who taught you? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, taught me. He said: Abd Allah wept until he wet the pebbles. He said: Recite as Umar taught you; Umar was for Islam a strong fortress."
"12851","He said: So I asked him about umm al-walad? He said: She is freed from her child's share."
"12852","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that Ibn Abbas said: An umm al-walad is not freed until freedom is pronounced for her."
"12853","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that Ibn al-Zubayr placed her in her son's share."
"12854","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar - I think - from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Concerning umm al-walad - by Allah, she is but like your camel or your sheep."
"12855","From Abu Sufyan, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man whose female slave bears him a child, she is freed after him."
"12856","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that Ibn al-Zubayr established Umm Hubayy, an umm walad of Muhammad ibn Suhayb, called Khalid, in her son's property."
"12857","From Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, that al-Hakam ibn Utayba informed him that Ali opposed Umar concerning umm al-walad: she is not freed when she bears her master's child."
"12858","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara informed me that Tawus informed him that Ibn Abbas said to a daughter of his belonging to an umm walad: I call you to witness that this one is free. He said: I think Tawus said: While she was playing on his belly. I told that to Mujahid, and he said: And I call you to witness that this one is free - his son al-Sabbah."
"12859","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me that Umar ibn al-Khattab met Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, with Umar his daughter Zaynab, mother of Abu Suraqa, and with Abd al-Rahman his son Uthman, both Zaynab and Uthman born of umm walads. Umar said: O Abu Muhammad, what have you done in this matter for Uthman? As for this one, Zaynab, I call you to witness she is free. Abd al-Rahman said: What are you saying? This is but Abd al-Rahman - what are you saying? Like one rebuking. Umar fell silent."
"12860","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida al-Salmani: It is said: I heard Ali saying: My opinion and Umar's opinion agreed concerning ummahat al-awlad: that they not be sold. He said: Then I later saw that they be sold. Abida said: I said to him: Your opinion along with Umar's in unity is dearer to me than your opinion alone in division - or he said: in fitna. He said: Ali laughed."
"12861","From Ubayd Allah and Abd Allah, the sons of Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar judged concerning ummahat al-awlad that they be neither sold, gifted, nor inherited; their owner enjoys them while alive, and when he dies she is freed."
"12862","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that Umar freed ummahat al-awlad when their masters die. From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Umar, like the hadith of al-Zuhri."
"12863","From al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: A group met him and said: Where have you come from? They said: From Iraq. He said: Whom did you meet? They said: Ibn al-Zubayr. They said: And he permitted us things forbidden to us. He said: What did he permit you of what was forbidden? They said: Sale of ummahat al-awlad. He said: Do you know Abu Hafs, Umar? He forbade that she be sold, gifted, or inherited, and said: Her owner enjoys her while alive, and when he dies she is free."
"12864","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Ibn al-Zubayr has permitted sale of ummahat al-awlad. Ibn Umar said: But Abu Hafs, Umar ibn al-Khattab, Commander of the Faithful - do you know him? - did not permit their sale, and he freed them."
"12865","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Umar freed ummahat al-awlad when their masters die."
"12866","From Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar freed ummahat al-awlad when their masters die; a woman of them came to Ali, her master wanting to sell her for a debt upon him, and he said: Go, Umar has freed you."
"12867","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man of the Ansar died leaving an umm walad; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed her, then received spoils and compensated her family."
"12868","From al-Thawri, from Ibn An'am, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: I said to Ibn al-Musayyib: Was it Umar who freed ummahat al-awlad? He said: No, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them."
"12869","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The veil was imposed upon Safiyya and Juwayriyya, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned for them as he apportioned for his wives."
"12870","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Ali settled debts on behalf of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after his death, most of them promises. He said: I think he said: five hundred thousand. Abd al-Razzaq said: Meaning dirhams. We said to Abd al-Razzaq: And how did he settle the debts of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeath that to him? He said: Yes, I do not doubt that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeathed to Ali; had it not been so, they would not have left him to settle."
"12871","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted that the mother of Ibrahim is free."
"12872","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Ajfa, that Umar said: A female slave, when she embraces Islam, is chaste and becomes protected, her child frees her; if she commits immorality and disbelieves - or he said: commits adultery - she returns to slavery."
"12873","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Iyas, that he wrote to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz concerning umm al-walad - meaning he held a view. He said: He showed me the return of the letter when it came to him; he wrote to him: Establish the hadd upon her; do not return her to him, and do not enslave."
"12874","From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata, concerning umm al-walad who commits adultery. He said: Her owner continues to enjoy her, and she is not sold."
"12875","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab was asked about umm al-walad who commits adultery: may her master sell her? He said: It is not right for him to sell her, but the hadd is established - the hadd of a female slave."
"12876","From Sufyan, from al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from Mujahid, he said: A hadd does not make her a slave."
"12877","And one informed me, from Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: A man said to Salim ibn Abd Allah: An umm walad of my father committed immorality. He said: Her immorality is upon herself; she is a free woman."
"12878","From Ma'mar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrima, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: A female slave is freed by her child, even if a miscarriage. From al-Thawri, from his father, from Ikrima, from Umar the like."
"12879","From al-Thawri, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: A miscarriage, if distinct, whether a lump of flesh or a clot."
"12880","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: If it is a distinct miscarriage."
"12881","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If she miscarries a distinct foetus, she is among ummahat al-awlad; if not distinct, she is a slave woman."
"12882","From Umar ibn Dharr, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi narrated to me that his father Abd Allah ibn Qarib bought a slave girl for four thousand, who had miscarried for a man; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab heard, and sent to him - and my father Abd Allah ibn Qarib was a friend of Umar ibn al-Khattab - and he blamed him severely and said: By Allah, I used to hold you above this or the like. He said: And he turned to the man beating him with the stick, saying: Now, when your flesh has mingled with theirs and your blood with theirs, you sell them and consume their prices. May Allah destroy the Jews; fat was forbidden to them - or he said: they forbade its fat - then they sold it and consumed its price. Return her. He said: So I returned her, recovered three thousand dirhams of my wealth, and a thousand was lost."
"12883","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If a female slave miscarries a distinct foetus, there is no way to sell her."
"12884","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man whose female slave bears him a child, then he marries her off, and she bears children. He said: They are owned."
"12885","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab said to me: They are owned. And Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan and the caliphs said: Free."
"12886","From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said concerning a female slave who bears her master a child, then he marries her off and she bears: Her child is not freed."
"12887","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that Rawh ibn Zinba took a slave girl of his as a concubine; she bore, then he married her to a male slave of his, and she bore him a child. He came to Abd al-Malik and mentioned that to him. He said: Her children are yours, alive and dead."
"12888","From Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When she is freed, her child is freed; they are freed by her freeing. Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar the like."
"12889","From Ibn Jurayj, al-Thawri, and Ibn Uyayna, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When she is freed, her child is freed. From Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Urwa al-Atwari, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, that he said concerning children of umm al-walad: like the saying of Ibn al-Musayyib."
"12890","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatada, both said: If her master marries her off after she has borne him a child, her child is in the status of his mother."
"12891","From al-Thawri, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi and others, he said: They are in the status of their mother. Al-Thawri said: And Ibrahim says that also - and the mudabbara and mukataba."
"12892","From Ma'mar, from Qatada: Concerning a female slave whom a man marries, and she bears him a child, then her husband buys her: Let him sell her if he wishes, unless he bought her while pregnant, or she bore him a child after he bought her. Ma'mar said: And Hammad said it from al-Nakha'i also."
"12893","From Ma'mar, he said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: She is among ummahat al-awlad. He said: And al-Hasan's saying is dearer to me."
"12894","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: She is a slave woman until she newly conceives in his possession."
"12895","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan or another, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said she had committed adultery. A man said: She is jealous, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, I shall swear to you that the merchant is wicked, and that a jealous person does not know the top of the valley from its bottom."
"12896","From Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan, that a woman found her husband with a slave girl of hers; she became jealous and went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he followed her until he caught up with her. She said: She committed adultery. He said: She lies, O Messenger of Allah, but such and such happened, and she seized his beard. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked her, and she released him. He said: She does not now know the top of the valley from its bottom."
"12897","From al-Thawri, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayya ibn Adi, that a woman came to Ali and said her husband had intercourse with her slave girl. He said: If you are truthful, we shall stone him; if you are lying, we shall flog you. She said: O woe to her, a jealous, fretful woman. He said: The prayer was established, and she went away."
"12898","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Ali ibn Abi Talib has proposed to al-Awra, daughter of Abu Jahl; that was not his right, and the daughter of Allah's Prophet and the daughter of Allah's enemy shall not be joined."
"12899","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ja'far, he said: Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Ali has proposed to al-Awra, daughter of Abu Jahl; it was not his right that the daughter of Allah's Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the daughter of Allah's enemy be joined; Fatima is but from me."
"12900","From Ibn Uyayna, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about the daughter of Abu Jahl, having proposed to her through her uncle al-Harith ibn Hisham. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: About which of her concerns do you ask me - about her lineage? He said: No, but I want to marry her; do you dislike that? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatima is but a part of me, and I dislike that she be grieved or angered. Ali said: I shall never do anything that displeases you."
"12901","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, and from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, going so far as promising marriage; that reached Fatima, and she said to her father: People claim you do not become angry for your daughters; this Abu al-Hasan has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, going so far as being promised marriage. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to address, praised Allah the Exalted and extolled Him as He deserves, then mentioned Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, praising him as an in-law, then said: Fatima is but a part of me, and I fear they will tempt her. By Allah, the daughter of Allah's Messenger and the daughter of Allah's enemy shall never be joined under one man. He said: Ali then fell silent about that marriage and abandoned it."
"12902","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Layth, from Abu Ubayda ibn Abd Allah, he said: I do not know whether he raised it or not? He said: Allah has made lawful no lawful thing more hateful to Him than divorce; Allah the Exalted has prescribed jihad upon men and jealousy upon women; whoever of them is patient shall have reward like that of a mujahid."
"12903","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ja'far, he said: Abu Bakr gave Ali a slave girl; Umm Ayman came in to Fatima and saw in her something she disliked. She said: What is wrong with you? She did not tell her. She said: What is wrong with you? By Allah, your father never concealed anything from me. She said: A slave girl given to Abu Hasan. Umm Ayman went out and called at the door of the house in which Ali was, at the top of her voice: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not to be honored in his family? He said: What is this voice? They said: Umm Ayman, saying: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not to be honored in his family? Ali said: And what is that? She said: A slave girl sent to you. Ali said: The slave girl belongs to Fatima."
"12904","From Ibn Uyayna, from one of their shaykhs, from his father, he said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah came to Umar complaining to him of what he suffers from women. Umar said: We find that too, so that when I want something, she says: You go only to the young woman of the sons of so-and-so, looking at them. Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud said to him: Has it not reached you that Ibrahim (peace be upon him) complained to Allah of Sarah's harsh character, and it was said to him: She was created from a rib; endure her as she is, so long as you see no defect in her religion. Umar said to him: Allah has indeed filled much knowledge between your ribs."
"12905","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came forth from marriage, not from fornication."
"12906","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to join the children of shirk to their fathers."
"12907","From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Awn, from Ghadirah al-Anbari, he said: We came to Umar ibn al-Khattab concerning women who traded among themselves in the Jahiliyyah, and he ordered that their children be valued against their fathers, and that they not be enslaved; tabaya'na means they sold."
"12908","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: Ihsan is that he has intercourse with her; nothing less than that is ihsan; and none is stoned until they testify: we saw him concealing (his organ) in that part of her; and Amr and Ibn Tawus said the same."
"12909","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: concerning an unmarried man who marries then commits zina before consummating with his wife, he said: flogging is upon him, and no stoning."
"12910","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab told me, concerning a man who committed zina though he was muhsan but had not touched his wife, he said: he is not stoned, but is flogged one hundred."
"12911","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man who marries a woman then commits zina before consummating with her, they said: it is not ihsan until he consummates with her. Mamar said: I know of no one who opposed their saying. He said: And it reached me that none is stoned until they testify: we saw him concealing (his organ) in that part of her."
"12912","From al-Thawri, he said: Ihsan is only by intercourse. Then he said: Samak ibn Harb told me, from Hanash, from Ali, that a man who had committed zina was brought to him, and he said: did you consummate with your wife? He said: No. So he beat him (flogged him)."
"12913","From Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash, he said: A man who had committed zina with a woman was brought to Ali, though he had married a wife but had not consummated; he said: did you commit zina? He said: I am not muhsan. So he ordered him, and he was flogged one hundred."
"12914","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Ala ibn Badr, he said: A woman committed immorality in the time of Ali ibn Abi Talib, though she had married but had not been consummated with; Ali was brought her, so he flogged her one hundred and banished her for a year to Nahr Karbala."
"12915","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: Marriage to a slave woman is not ihsan."
"12916","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Nakhai, they said: A slave woman does not make a free man muhsan."
"12917","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: A free man is not made muhsan by a slave woman; Ibrahim said it."
"12918","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: A slave woman becomes muhsana by a free man."
"12919","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab told me, concerning a man who committed zina though he had consummated with a slave woman, he said: hadd; the hadd of the muhsan is stoning by way of hadd if he is free."
"12920","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan asked Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud: does a slave woman make a free man muhsan? He said: Yes. He said: From whom? He said: We found the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying that."
"12921","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, he said: Marriage to a slave woman is not ihsan."
"12922","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: A slave's marriage to a free woman is not ihsan."
"12923","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Nakhai, he said: A slave does not make a free woman muhsana."
"12924","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib and al-Hasan, they said: A slave makes a free woman muhsana."
"12925","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Nakhai, concerning a slave who married a woman then was freed, then committed zina before consummating with her, they said: he is flogged and there is no stoning upon him; and Qatadah said: he is stoned."
"12926","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning two slaves who married then were freed, then committed immorality before consummating with her, he said: they are flogged; and another said: if he consummated with her then they committed zina, he is stoned and she is stoned."
"12927","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: Marriage to a woman of the People of the Book is ihsan."
"12928","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, they said: A Jewish woman and a Christian woman make a Muslim muhsan."
"12929","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, he said: Marriage to the People of the Book is ihsan."
"12930","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, he said: It is ihsan."
"12931","From Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: It is ihsan."
"12932","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: A free man is not made muhsan by a Christian woman; and Ibrahim said it."
"12933","From Ibrahim ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, he said: A Jewish woman nor a Christian woman makes a Muslim muhsan, while he makes them muhsana."
"12934","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who became muhsan in shirk then commits zina in Islam, he said: it is not ihsan until he attains her in Islam; and al-Zuhri said: he is stoned, because he was muhsan."
"12935","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, and from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, they said: His ihsan in shirk is nothing until he covers her (consummates) in Islam."
"12936","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who marries while a mushrik and consummates with his wife, then becomes Muslim, then commits zina, he said: he is stoned because he was muhsan, if he was of the People of the Book; and if he was not of the People of the Book, then not; and Qatadah said: he is stoned."
"12937","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who married a woman then consummated with her, and she turns out to be his milk sister, he said: it is not ihsan; and Mamar from Qatadah said it."
"12938","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: The unmarried man is flogged one hundred and exiled a year."
"12939","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Tawus told me, from his father, that he said concerning the unmarried man who commits zina: he is flogged one hundred and banished a year."
"12940","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: It was revealed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he said: Take! Take! Allah has made a way for them: married with married, one hundred flogging and stoning; and virgin with virgin, one hundred flogging and a year's exile. He said: And al-Hasan used to give fatwa by it."
"12941","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah and from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a laborer for this man, and he committed zina with his wife; I was told my son deserves stoning, so I ransomed him with a slave girl and one hundred sheep; then the people of knowledge told me: upon my son is one hundred flogging and a year's banishment, and upon this man's wife is stoning, as I deem; he said: So judge between us by the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: As for the sheep and the slave girl, they are returned to you; as for your son, upon him is one hundred flogging and a year's banishment. Then he said to a man of Banu Aslam called Unays: Rise, O Unays, and go to this man's wife; if she confesses, stone her."
"12942","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibn Shihab told me, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I adjure you by Allah, judge for me only by the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic. The other disputant, who was more understanding than he, said: Yes, judge between us by the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, and permit me. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Speak. He said: My son was a laborer for this man and committed zina with his wife; I was told my son deserves stoning, so I ransomed him with one hundred sheep and a slave girl; then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me: upon my son is only one hundred flogging and a year's banishment, and upon his wife is stoning. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall judge between you by the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic: the sheep and the slave girl are returned to you, and upon your son is one hundred flogging and a year's banishment. And go in the morning, O Unays, to this man's wife, for a man of Aslam; if she confesses, stone her. So he went to her in the morning, and she confessed; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her, and she was stoned."
"12943","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, that a man fell upon an unmarried slave girl and impregnated her, and she confessed though he was not muhsan; Abu Bakr ordered him, and he was flogged one hundred, then was exiled. From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, the same."
"12944","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said concerning the unmarried man who commits zina with the unmarried woman: they are flogged one hundred and exiled a year. Ibrahim said: They are not exiled to one village; each of them is exiled to a village. And Ali said: Exile suffices them as protection from temptation."
"12945","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Upon slaves there is no exile, nor stoning. Mamar said: And I heard Hammad saying that."
"12946","From Uthman, from Said, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Ali said concerning the umm al-walad: when her master frees her or dies leaving her, then she commits zina, she is flogged and not exiled; and Ibn Masud said: she is flogged and exiled, and not stoned."
"12947","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar executed the hadd upon a slave girl of his for zina, and exiled her to Fadak."
"12948","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Upon slaves, male and female, is flogging, whether they married or not; and al-Zuhri used to say: ihsan can be upon one other than the married, being chastity."
"12949","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and Allah and His Messenger have decreed: if four testify against two unmarried ones, they are flogged as Allah, mighty and majestic, said: one hundred lashes, and let no pity seize you for them in Allah's religion; and they are banished a year from the land they were in, and their banishment is separate. And it was said: the first hadd established in Islam was for a man brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who had stolen, and testimony was borne against him; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to be cut; when the man was surrounded, he looked at the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as though ashes had been strewn in it. The man said: O Messenger of Allah! As though cutting him weighs hard upon you. He said: What prevents me, while you are helpers of Satan against your brother? They said: Then release him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me? The Imam, when a hadd is brought to him, ought not suspend it."
"12950","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When the two adulterers are exiled, each of them is exiled to a village."
"12951","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Abu Bakr ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf was banished for wine to Khaybar, then he joined Heraclius and became Christian. Umar said: I shall never banish a Muslim after him. And from Ibrahim, that Ali said: Exile suffices them as protection from temptation."
"12952","From Mamar, he said: And he was asked: how far is the adulterer exiled? I heard al-Zuhri: Umar exiled from Madinah to Basrah, and from Madinah to Khaybar. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating this hadith."
"12953","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, that Ali exiled from Kufah to Basrah. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating this hadith."
"12954","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq: I said to Ata: banishment from Makkah to Taif? He said: That suffices him."
"12955","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar exiled to Fadak."
"12956","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said concerning the unmarried woman who commits zina with the unmarried man: they are flogged one hundred and exiled. He said: And Ali said: Exile suffices them as protection from temptation."
"12957","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Abu Bakr exiled to Fadak, and Umar."
"12958","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Umar saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the truth, and sent down the Book with him; among what was sent down upon him was the verse of stoning. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned, and we stoned after him. I fear that time will grow long upon the people, and a speaker will say: By Allah, we do not find stoning in the Book of Allah, and they will go astray abandoning an ordinance Allah revealed. Indeed stoning is true upon whoever commits zina, when he is muhsan, and proof stands, or there is pregnancy, or confession."
"12959","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: A man of Muzaynah told me, while we were with Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The first stoned one the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned was of the Jews who committed zina, a man of them and a woman. Their scholars conferred before raising their matter to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and some said to others: This Prophet was sent with lightening; we know stoning was obligated in the Torah. Come, let us ask this Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about our two companions who committed zina after being muhsan: if he gives us a fatwa less than stoning, we accept it and take the lightening, and argue with it before Allah when we meet Him, saying: we accepted the fatwa of a Prophet of Your Prophets; and if he orders us with stoning, we disobey him, though we have disobeyed Allah in what He wrote upon us, that stoning is in the Torah. They came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he sat in the mosque among his Companions, and said: O Abu al-Qasim, what deem you of a man of them and a woman who committed zina after being muhsan? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rose and gave them nothing in reply, and men of the Muslims rose with him until they came to the Jews' house of study, where they studied the Torah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at the door and said: O company of Jews, I adjure you by Allah Who sent down the Torah upon Musa, what find you in the Torah for one who commits zina when muhsan? They said: He is blackened and paraded. They said: And blackening is that the two adulterers are carried upon a donkey, their backs faced to each other, and they are paraded. He said: And their learned man, a young youth, fell silent; when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him, he pressed him. Their learned man said: O Allah, since you adjured us, we find stoning in the Torah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What was the first thing by which you lightened Allah's command? They said: A man of us, a kinsman of one of our kings, committed zina, so he imprisoned him and delayed stoning from him; then another committed zina after him, of a family of the people, and the king wanted to stone him, but his folk stood in his way, or he said: folk rose for him, and said: By Allah, our companion shall not be stoned until you bring your companion and stone him. So they made this punishment between them. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I judge by what is in the Torah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them, and they were stoned. Al-Zuhri said: Salim told me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw them when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered their stoning; when it came, I saw him shielding her with his hand, to guard her from the stones. It reached us that this verse was sent down about him: We sent down the Torah, wherein is guidance and light; the Prophets who submitted judge by it for those who are Jews; and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was of them."
"12960","From Mamar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when two Jews who had committed zina were brought; he sent for their reader, and he came with the Torah; he asked him: Do you find stoning in your Book? They said: No, but they are paraded and blackened. He said: Then he said, or it was said to him: Read. He placed his hand upon the verse of stoning, and read around it. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Move your palm. He moved his palm, and there was the verse of stoning. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them, and they were stoned. Ibn Umar said: I saw them stoned, and he shields her from the stones."
"12961","From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Jews came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a man of them and a woman who had committed zina. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: How deal you with one of you who commits zina? They said: We beat them. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What find you in the Torah? They said: We find nothing in it. Abdullah ibn Salam said: You lie; in the Torah is stoning. Bring the Torah and read it, if you are truthful. They brought the Torah, and their teacher who taught it placed his palm upon the verse of stoning, and read what was above his hand and behind it, and did not read the verse of stoning. Abdullah ibn Salam pulled his hand from the verse of stoning and said: What is this? When they saw that, he said: It is the verse of stoning. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them, and they were stoned, where funerals are placed. Abdullah said: I saw her companion bending over her, to guard her from the stones."
"12962","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a man of Aslam, and a Jewish man, and a woman."
"12963","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata told me that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I committed zina. He turned away from him, then he said it a second time, and he turned away, then he said it a third time, and he turned away, then he said it a fourth; he said: Stone him. Ata said: He panicked and fled; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told, and they said: He fled, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why did you not leave him? Hence they say: when he retracts after the four, he is excused and not stoned; and when he confesses before other than the Imam, it is nothing, until he confesses before the Imam four times."
"12964","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When he confesses zina then denies, he is not hadd-punished, even if he confessed several times."
"12965","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab told me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that a man of Aslam came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him he had committed zina, testifying against himself four testimonies; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him, and he was stoned; and he had been muhsan; they claim he was Maiz ibn Malik. Ibn Jurayj said: Yahya ibn Said told me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, freedman of Ibn Umar, that it reached him: a man of Aslam came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Avoid this filth which Allah forbade; whoever falls into any of it, let him conceal himself."
"12966","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that a man of Aslam came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and confessed zina; he turned away from him, then he confessed, and he turned away, until he testified against himself four times. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Are you mad? He said: No. He said: Were you muhsan? He said: Yes. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him, and he was stoned at the prayer place; when the stones pained him, he fled, was caught, and was stoned till he died. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke good of him, and did not pray over him. Mamar said: Ibn Tawus told me, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told that he fled, he said: Why did you not leave him, or he said: Would you had left him! Mamar said: Ayyub told me, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned the Aslami, he said: Conceal from me of your private faults what Allah has concealed; whoever commits any of it, let him conceal himself."
"12967","From Mamar: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir told me, from Ikrimah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Maiz when he confessed zina: Did you kiss? Did you touch?"
"12968","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr told me: Ayyub told me, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr the day Maiz was struck, and lengthened the first two of Zuhr till the people nearly failed from the long standing; when he finished, he ordered him to be stoned, and he was stoned, but was not killed, till Umar ibn al-Khattab threw him with a camel's jawbone, struck his head, and killed him. He said: Maiz's soul departed. It was said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Messenger of Allah! Do you pray over him? He said: No. When the morrow came, he prayed Zuhr, and lengthened the first two rakahs as he had lengthened them yesterday, or a little less; when he finished, he said: Pray over your companion. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people prayed over him."
"12969","From Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr told me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Samit, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard him saying: The Aslami came to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and testified against himself that he had attained a free woman unlawfully, four times, each time he turned away from him; on the fifth he faced him. He said: Did you penetrate her? He said: Yes. He said: Until that of you disappeared in that of her, as the kohl stick disappears in the kohl container, and the rope in the well? He said: Yes. He said: Do you know what zina is? He said: Yes; I did with her unlawfully what a man does with his wife lawfully. He said: What want you by this statement? He said: I want you to purify me. So he ordered him, and he was stoned. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard two men of his Companions, one saying to his fellow: Look at this whom Allah had covered, yet his soul left him not till he was stoned like a dog. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent toward them, till he passed a donkey's carcass with its leg raised. He said: Where are so-and-so and so-and-so? They said: We are here, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Go down and eat of this donkey's carcass. They said: O Prophet of Allah! May Allah forgive you, who eats of this? He said: What you just took of your brother's honor is worse than eating carrion. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, he is now in the rivers of Paradise, plunging in them."
"12970","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, he said: Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he sent him back four times; he sent him back, then ordered him, and he was stoned; when the stones touched him, he shifted and panicked; when it reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Would you had left him."
"12971","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that a man of Aslam came to Umar and said: The other man committed zina. He said: Repent to Allah, and cover with Allah's cover; Allah accepts repentance from His servants, and people excuse but do not revile. His soul left him not till he came to Abu Bakr, and he said to him the like of Umar's saying; his soul left him not till he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him; he turned away from him; he came to him from the other side, and he turned away; he came from the other side and mentioned that to him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to his family and asked them of him: Is he mad? Is there a wind (affliction) in him? They said: No. So he ordered him, and he was stoned. Ibn Uyaynah said: Abdullah ibn Dinar told me, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood upon the pulpit and said: O people, avoid this filth which Allah forbade you; whoever commits any of that, let him conceal himself. Yahya ibn Said said: From Nuaym ibn Abdillah ibn Hazzal, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Hazzal: Had you covered him with your garment, it had been better for you. He said: And Hazzal is the one who had ordered him to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and tell him."
"12972","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: Maiz ibn Malik, a short man in a waist-wrapper with no cloak upon him, was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was reclining upon a cushion on his left. He spoke to him, and I know not what he spoke to him, while I was far, with the people between me and him. He said: Take him away. Then he said: Bring him back. He spoke to him while I heard, though the people were between me and him. Then he said: Take him and stone him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood preaching, and said: Every time we go out in Allah's path, one of them stays behind, with bleating like a goat's bleating, granting one of them milk from the heap of milk. By Allah, by Allah, I shall get hold of none of them but I shall make an example of him."
"12973","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Maiz was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and confessed twice. Then he said: Take him away. Then he said: Bring him back. He confessed twice, till he confessed four times. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take him and stone him."
"12974","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that a woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and confessed zina against herself; he sent her back four times. On the fourth she said to him: O Messenger of Allah! Would you send me back as you sent back Maiz ibn Malik? He said: He delayed her till she delivered, then said: Suckle him. A man said: Its nursing is upon me. So he ordered her, and she was stoned."
"12975","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Shabi, he said: No hadd is executed upon a pregnant woman till she delivers."
"12976","From Mamar, and al-Thawri, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Imran, he said: A woman confessed before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of zina; he ordered her clothes tied over her, then stoned her, then prayed over her. Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah! You stoned her, then pray over her? He said: She repented a repentance that, had it been divided among seventy of Madinah's people, it would have encompassed them; and did you find anything better than that she gave her life for Allah?"
"12977","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, that a woman of Juhaynah confessed before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of zina, and said: I am pregnant. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called her guardian and said: Treat her well; when she delivers, tell me. He did so. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her clothes tied over her, then ordered her, and she was stoned, then he prayed over her. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah! You stoned her, yet pray over her? He said: She repented a repentance that, had it been divided among seventy of Madinah's people, it would have encompassed them; and did she find better than that she gave her life for Allah, mighty and majestic?"
"12978","From Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a woman, and some Muslims said: This woman's deed is void. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rather this is expiation for what she did, and you will be reckoned after for what you did. And Ibrahim mentioned it from Ibn al-Munkadir."
"12979","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu Juhayfah told me that al-Shabi told him that Ali was brought a pregnant woman of Hamdan, Sharahah by name; she had committed zina. Ali said to her: Perhaps the man forced you? She said: No. He said: Perhaps the man fell upon you while you slept? She said: No. He said: Perhaps you have a husband among these our enemies, and you conceal him? She said: No. So he detained her till she delivered; he flogged her Thursday, one hundred lashes, and stoned her Friday. He ordered a pit dug for her in the market; the people surrounded her, or he said: with her; he struck them with a stick, then said: Not thus is stoning; if you do this, some of you will kill others; but line up as you line for prayer. Then he said: O people, the first of the people to stone the adulterer is the Imam, when there is confession; and when four witnesses testify to zina, the first of the people to stone are the witnesses by their testimony against him, then the Imam, then the people. Then he threw her with a stone and said takbir; then he ordered the first row and said: Throw. Then he said: Disperse. And likewise row by row, till they killed her."
"12980","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ali dug for Sharahah al-Hamdaniyyah when he stoned her, and ordered her detained till she delivers."
"12981","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: A pit is dug for the stoned till part of him disappears."
"12982","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn and Ismail, from al-Shabi, he said: Ali was brought Sharahah; he flogged her Thursday and stoned her Friday, then said: Stoning is two stonings: secret stoning and public stoning. As for public stoning: the witnesses, then the Imam. As for secret stoning: confession, then the Imam, then the people."
"12983","Al-Thawri said: Ibn Harb, meaning Simak ibn Harb, told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla told me, from a man of Hudhayl counted among Quraysh, he said: I was with Ali when he stoned Sharahah, and I said: She died in an evil state. He struck me with a stick or a whip in his hand till it pained me. I said: You pained me. He said: Even if I pained you. He said: She shall never be asked about this sin of hers again, like a debt paid."
"12984","He said: Alqamah ibn Marthad told me, from al-Shabi, he said: When Ali stoned Sharahah, her kin came and said: How deal we with her? He said: Deal with her as you deal with your dead, meaning washing and praying over her."
"12985","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali flogged Thursday and stoned Friday, saying: I flog you by the Book of Allah, and stone you by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12986","From Israil, he said: Simak ibn Harb told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla told me, from a man of Hudhayl, he said: I heard Ali saying: Whoever does evil and the hadd is executed upon him, it is expiation."
"12987","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir, he said: Ali said concerning the previously married: I flog her by the Quran and stone her by the Sunnah. He said: And Ubayy ibn Kab said the same."
"12988","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Upon the stoned there is no flogging. It reached us that Umar stoned and did not flog."
"12989","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that he denied flogging with stoning, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned, and flogging was not mentioned."
"12990","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Hittan ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his face flushed for it. One day it was sent down upon him, and he met it; when he was relieved of it, he said: Take from me; Allah has made a way for them: married with married, one hundred flogging, then stoning with stones; and virgin with virgin, one hundred flogging, then a year's exile. From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abdillah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, the same."
"12991","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Masruq, he said: The two unmarried are flogged or exiled; the two married are stoned and not flogged; the two old ones are flogged and stoned."
"12992","From al-Thawri, he said: Concerning the married man who commits zina then is flogged while he deems that grave, then he learns of it, he said: he is stoned. He said: Abu Husayn told me of it, from al-Shabi, that Ali flogged and stoned."
"12993","From al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Ubayy ibn Kab said to me: How much recite you of Surat al-Ahzab? He said: I said: Seventy-three, or seventy-four. He said: Only that? It used to nearly equal Surat al-Baqarah, or it was longer; and in it was the verse of stoning. He said: I said: Abu al-Mundhir! What is the verse of stoning? He said: When the old man and the old woman commit zina, stone them outright, as exemplary punishment from Allah; and Allah is Mighty, Wise. Al-Thawri said: And it reached us that men of the Prophet's Companions, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who recited the Quran, were struck on the day of Musaylamah, and letters of the Quran were lost."
"12994","From Mamar, from Ibn Judan, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab ordered a caller, who called: prayer is assembled. Then he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, be not deceived away from the verse of stoning; it was sent down in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, and we recited it; but it went away with much Quran that went away with Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the sign of that is that he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned, and Abu Bakr stoned, and I stoned after them. There shall come folk of this ummah who deny stoning, deny the sun rising from the west, deny intercession, deny the Hawd, deny the Dajjal, deny the torment of the grave, and deny folk coming out of the Fire after entering it."
"12995","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ali ibn Husayn told me that he heard Abu al-Shatha saying: Ibn Abbas did not deem stoning upon a woman though three men, with her husband as fourth, testified zina against her; he says: he does lian with her. He said: And Abu al-Shatha said: I deem her stoned."
"12996","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a woman against whom four testified zina, one of them her husband, he said: Her husband does lian with her, and the three are flogged. He said: And al-Zuhri said: She is stoned."
"12997","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, he said: When they are four, one the husband, they protect their backs, and the hadd is executed. He said: And Ibrahim said: They are beaten till a fourth besides the husband comes with them."
"12998","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man who accuses his wife and brings three who testify, they said: They are flogged, and her husband does not do lian with her."
"12999","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who accuses his wife and brings three who testify, and they are flogged the hadd, then he brings two men who testify, he said: They are flogged, and he is hadd-punished with them, because he followed with testimony contradicting the truth after the penalties fell; as though he means the husband had done lian, then brought witnesses."
"13000","From al-Thawri, from Salim, from Ibrahim, he said: Wabarah asked him about three men and two women who testified against a woman for zina, and he said: No, except thus, pointing with four fingers, saying: except the four."
"13001","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: If six women testified to zina with a man? He said: No, except three men and two women."
"13002","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Hujayr told me, from one he approves, as though Ibn Tawus: he permits women's testimony with men in everything except zina, because they ought not look at that. He said: And a man ought to look at that till he knows it."
"13003","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man against whom six women and a man testify zina, he said: Their testimony is not allowed therein. He said: Women's testimony is not allowed in a hadd, nor marriage, nor divorce."
"13004","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: Women's testimony is not allowed in hudud, nor a man's testimony upon a man's testimony, nor surety in a hadd."
"13005","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said: Women's testimony is not allowed in hudud."
"13006","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who accuses a man then brings three who testify, he said: They are flogged, and he is flogged, unless he brings four; if he brings four and they all testify, the hadd is executed."
"13007","From al-Thawri, from Bayan, from Ibrahim, he said: They are beaten till he brings a fourth."
"13008","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who accused his wife and brought three, and they were flogged the hadd, then he brought two men who testified, he said: They are flogged, and he is hadd-punished with them, because he followed with testimony contradicting the truth after the penalties fell; as though he means the husband had done lian, then brought two men."
"13009","From al-Thawri, from al-Shabi, concerning four witnesses against a woman for zina, and she is found virgin, he said: I strike her, and upon her is her Lord's seal; so he left her and averted the hadd from her."
"13010","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, concerning four who testified against a woman for zina then differed about the place, some saying: in Kufah, and some saying: in Basrah, he said: it is averted from all of them."
"13011","From Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab told me, concerning a woman against whom four upright witnesses testify zina, and four upright come testifying by Allah that she was with us the night these testified they saw her commit zina, and that these are lying sinners, both groups upright whose testimony is accepted, he said: their uprightness is equal. He said: Those who accused her are hadd-punished, when they name one night without differing therein."
"13012","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Said ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the (female) rider and the ridden."
"13013","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibn Shihab told me, he said: I found our scholars saying concerning a woman who comes to a woman with thigh-rubbing and the like: both are flogged, one hundred each, the doer and the done-to."
"13014","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a woman who comes to a woman with thigh-rubbing, he said: Both are flogged, each of them one hundred."
"13015","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A previously married man testified against himself three times, then retracted before completing four or uttering takbir. He said: They are made an example of, other than hadd. Ibn Jurayj said: And I say: he mentioned the matter of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah on which Abd al-Malik ruled. And Ibn Jurayj said: I heard one of our companions narrating of a woman in Yemen who confessed zina against herself; Muhammad ibn Yusuf wrote about her to Abd al-Malik, who wrote: detain her a year, then ask her every three months; if she confesses four times, stone her. She confessed after three, or six, or nine months, then was made an example of after twelve months and left; we deem her first confession in his view was nothing."
"13016","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who confesses then denies, he said: No hadd is executed upon him when he denies after his confession, even if he confessed four times."
"13017","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who testified against himself three or four times then was punished exemplarily, he said: Upon him is no tazir nor anything. Abd al-Razzaq said: And the people hold it."
"13018","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: He testified against himself that he stole once, then retracted. He said: Detain him. I said: Why is it not like zina, that he testify twice against himself for theft? He said: It is not like it. It was said about that, and it was not said about this."
"13019","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When he confesses after punishment, he is not taken by it in a hadd or otherwise."
"13020","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When a free man commits zina with a slave woman, he is stoned if he was muhsan."
"13021","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: He is not stoned when an unmarried or married man commits zina with a slave woman; both are flogged one hundred and exiled a year. He said: And likewise if a free woman commits zina with a slave. And he used to say otherwise before that, till he heard Habib ibn Thabit saying that, then he said it."
"13022","From al-Thawri, he said: Concerning the free man who commits zina with the slave woman, upon him is stoning, if he was muhsan."
"13023","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: A boy married a woman before reaching emission, then committed zina after that; is he stoned? He said: I do not deem him stoned till he emits when he attains her. I said: Two men testify: we saw him upon her belly, intending thereby (to prove zina)? He said: They are punished exemplarily. Ibn Jurayj said, and I say: they are not hadd-punished, because they did not testify to zina, but are punished exemplarily."
"13024","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Hammad, concerning a girl whose husband consummated with her though she had not menstruated, then she committed immorality, they said: If the like of her menstruates, the hadd is due upon her, else not."
"13025","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning children, he said: Upon them is no hadd till they have wet dreams, or slave girls menstruate; and whoever accuses them bears no hadd, because hudud are not due upon them, so no hadd upon whoever accuses them, when he accuses them specifically, not mentioning their fathers nor their mothers."
"13026","From al-Thawri, he said: We heard that the (wet) dream is at earliest fourteen, at latest eighteen; when hudud come, the latest is taken."
"13027","From al-Thawri, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Hibban, he said: Ibn Abi al-Sabah courted a woman in his poetry, and he was raised to Umar. He said: Look at his waist-wrapper; he had not grown hair. He said: Had you grown pubic hair, I would have flogged you the hadd."
"13028","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, that a boy who had stolen was brought to Uthman. He said: Look at his waist-wrapper. They looked and found he had not grown hair, so he was not cut."
"13029","From al-Thawri, from Abu Salamah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: A girl who had not menstruated and had stolen was brought, and he did not cut her."
"13030","From al-Thawri, concerning the minor who attains (intercourse) but does not emit, he said: Upon him is no hadd, nor upon her, till he has a wet dream."
"13031","From al-Thawri, he said: If he attains her though she is previously married and he is minor, or he is adult and she is minor, the hadd is executed upon her, and not executed upon her; and if a minor deflowers a virgin, he is hadd-punished, and the dower is upon him in his wealth, not upon the aqilah."
"13032","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, from al-Hasan, he said: The hadd is executed upon the two adults, when a minor attains an adult woman, or an adult attains a minor girl."
"13033","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The hadd is executed upon the adult, and upon the minor there is no hadd."
"13034","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man who divorces his wife thrice before two witnesses while absent, then comes and enters upon his wife and attains her, and the two witnesses testify: we witnessed that he divorced her, they said: he is hadd-punished one hundred, and they are separated; and if he denies, saying: By Allah, these two testified falsely against me, and if he admits that he had divorced her, he is stoned."
"13035","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who divorces thrice then enters upon her, he said: The hadd is averted from her, and the dower is upon her."
"13036","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Jarir, from Isa, from Asim, from Shurayh, that a man divorced his wife thrice, and folk testified against him that he had intercourse with her after that. He said: If you wish, testify that he is an adulterer."
"13037","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who divorces his wife thrice, then a man gives him fatwa to take her back, and he enters upon her, he said: The one who gave him fatwa is punished exemplarily, and he is separated from his wife, and fined the dower."
"13038","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who divorces his wife thrice then attains her, denying he divorced her, but divorce is testified against him, he said: They are separated, and upon him is neither stoning nor punishment. Ibn Jurayj said: And it reached me that Umar ibn al-Khattab ruled that. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa and others told me that Abd al-Malik ruled likewise."
"13039","From Uthman, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who says to his wife: I saw you commit zina before I married you, he said: he is flogged, and there is no lian between them; and Qatadah said: Al-Hasan and Zurarah ibn Awfa said: he does lian with her; it is people's saying; thus said Ibn Abi Awfa."
"13040","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who accuses his wife and establishes proof against her, and she is stoned, he said: He inherits her."
"13041","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When a man is flogged in a hadd, then repentance is perceived of him, and a man taunts him with it, he is punished exemplarily."
"13042","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told concerning a man flogged for zina then repented, he said: No hadd upon one who accused him."
"13043","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: Ali said: Whoever is charged with zina is punished exemplarily, even if truthful."
"13044","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Had a man incurred a hadd in shirk then became Muslim, and a man taunts him with it in Islam, he is punished exemplarily; and he said concerning the slave, the slave woman, the Christian man and woman: their accuser is punished exemplarily."
"13045","From al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabus ibn Mukhariq, that Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr wrote to Ali asking him about two Muslims who became heretics, a Muslim who committed zina with a Christian woman, and a mukatab who left a remainder of his contract and left free children. Ali wrote to him: As for the two who became heretics, if they repent, else strike their necks; as for the Muslim, execute the hadd upon him, and hand the Christian woman to her co-religionists; as for the mukatab, the remainder of his contract is paid, and what remains is for his free children."
"13046","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning a man who trod his wife's slave girl: if he forced her, she is free, and he owes her like; and if she obeyed him, she belongs to him, and he owes her mistress her like. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard al-Hasan al-Basri narrating from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same."
"13047","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Amir ibn Matar al-Shaybani, he said: Ibn Masud said: If he forced her, she is freed, and he is fined her like; and if she obeyed him, he keeps her, and is fined her like."
"13048","From Israil ibn Yunus: Simak ibn Harb told him, from Mabad and Ubayd, sons of Humran, that Abdullah struck him less than the hadd, and did not stone him."
"13049","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Simak, from Mabad and Ubayd, sons of Humran ibn Dhuhl, they said: Ibn Masud passed by a man who said: I committed zina. He said: Then we stone you, if you are muhsan. He said: It was his wife's slave girl he came to. Abdullah said: If you forced her, free her, and give your wife a slave girl in her place. He said: By Allah, I forced her and beat her. He said: So he did not stone him, and ordered him, and he was beaten less than the hadd."
"13050","From al-Thawri, from Nusayr, from Ibrahim, he said: He is rebuked (tazir), and no hadd."
"13051","From al-Thawri, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, that Ibn Mas'ud said: We do not see any hadd on him, nor any dower-compensation."
"13052","From al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ali said: If he were brought to me I would stone him — meaning the one who has intercourse with his wife's slave girl. Ibn Mas'ud does not know what happened after him."
"13053","From al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: If the one who has intercourse with his wife's slave girl were brought to me, I would stone him, when he is muhṣan."
"13054","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I do not care whether I had intercourse with my wife's slave girl or with the slave girl of Awsajah, a man of al-Nakha'."
"13055","From Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: I do not care whether I had intercourse with my wife's slave girl or with a slave girl of al-Nakha'."
"13056","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: A man went out on a journey, and his wife sent with him a slave girl of hers to serve him, so he charged her value against himself and had intercourse with her. His case was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: You have sold one of your hands to the other. So he flogged him one hundred and did not stone him. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, the like of it, except that he said: He was sick and she used to attend to him — meaning the private parts."
"13057","From Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani informed me, he said: I passed by Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and with him was a man telling him hadith, so he called me and said: When we hear a strange report we like to let you hear it, and when you two hear one we like you to narrate it. Then he said to me: Ask him — meaning the man with him — about what he narrates. The man said: Uthman sent a charity-collector to Banu Sa'd ibn Hudayr, and while he was collecting, a man said to his wife, and with her was a slave girl, he said to his wife: Give charity on behalf of your freed girl — meaning the slave girl. His wife said: Rather give charity on behalf of your daughter. The collector said: What is the matter with her? The man said: The mother of this slave girl was a slave woman of this wife of mine, and I had intercourse with her, and she gave birth to this slave girl. The collector said: I shall raise you until I bring you to the Commander of the Faithful. He said: If the Commander of the Faithful has already judged concerning us. The collector said: And what did he judge concerning you? He said: His case was raised to Umar, the Commander of the Faithful, and he flogged him one hundred and did not stone him. He said: I do not know it except that he said: So the collector asked about that and found it as the man had told him."
"13058","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who committed zina with his wife's young slave girl, he said: He is flogged and not stoned."
"13059","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Whoever commits zina with his wife's young slave girl is stoned."
"13060","From Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani, he said: A man who committed zina with his wife's slave girl was raised to Umar, so he flogged him one hundred and did not stone him."
"13061","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, he said: It was mentioned to Ali that a man says: There is no harm if a man has intercourse with his wife's young slave girl. He said: If he were brought to us we would smash his head with a rock."
"13062","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning the one who has intercourse with his wife's young slave girl, he said: It is zina."
"13063","From Amr ibn Hawshab, he said: I asked Ata ibn Abi Rabah about a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave girl, then a man slandered him and said: O adulterer. There is no hadd on his slanderer."
"13064","From al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, that a woman came to Ali and said: Her husband had intercourse with her slave girl. He said: If you are truthful we shall stone him, and if you are lying we shall flog you eighty. She said: O woe to her, jealous and indignant. He said: The prayer was established, and she went away. He said: And a man came and said: O Commander of the Faithful! The cow? He said: For seven. He said: The horn? He said: It will not harm you. He said: The lame? He said: When it reaches the place of sacrifice. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine closely the eye and the ear."
"13065","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: There was a daughter of Kharijah under Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, then she married after him ... and she gifted her to him, so Umar flogged her the hadd of slander."
"13066","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr informed me, that Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Abu Bakr, and she was Ansari through her mother, informed him, that Habibah bint Kharijah sent a slave girl of hers with a husband of hers from the Ansar, called Habib ibn Isaf, to al-Sham, and said: She is in al-Sham, spend on her, and sell her as you see fit. And she said: She will wash your clothes, look after your baggage, and serve you. So he went and bought her for himself, then returned with her to Medina pregnant. The daughter of Kharijah came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and denied that she had ordered him to sell her, so Umar was about to stone her husband, until her people spoke to her, and she said: O Allah, now I testify that I had ordered him to sell her. So she affirmed that to Umar, and he struck her eighty."
"13067","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that a woman came to Umar and said: Her husband committed zina with her young slave girl. The man said to Umar: The woman gifted her to me. Umar said: You shall surely bring proof, or I shall smash your head with stones. When the woman saw that, she said: He has spoken the truth; I had gifted her to him, but jealousy carried me. So Umar flogged her the hadd and let him go."
"13068","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: I was with Umar ibn al-Khattab when a man came to him and said: My slave committed zina with my wife, and she, this one, confesses. Abu Waqid said: So he sent me to her and said: Ask this man's wife about what he said. He said: So I went, and there was a young girl newly mature, dressed in her clothes, sitting in her courtyard. I said to her: Your husband came to the Commander of the Faithful and told him that you committed zina with his slave, and the Commander of the Faithful sent me to ask you about that. Abu Waqid said: If you did not do it, there is no harm on you. She was silent for a while, then I said — Abu Waqid is the speaker: O Allah, loose her mouth today for whatever You will. She said: By Allah, I shall not combine indecency and lying. Then she said: He has spoken the truth. So Umar ordered concerning her, and she was stoned."
"13069","From al-Thawri, concerning the slave who commits zina with his master's wife, he said: The hadd is carried out on her."
"13070","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: A woman who gave birth after six months was raised to Umar, so he asked the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her. Ali said: Do you not see that He says: And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months. And He said: And his weaning is in two years. So pregnancy here is six months. So he left her. Then he said: It reached us that she gave birth to another after six months."
"13071","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn al-Aswad al-Dili, from his father, he said: A woman who gave birth after six months was raised to Umar, and Umar wanted to stone her. Her sister came to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Umar is stoning my sister, so I adjure you by Allah, if you know that she has an excuse, to tell me of it. Ali said: She has an excuse. So she uttered a takbir which Umar heard from where he was. She went to Umar and said: Ali claims that my sister has an excuse. Umar sent to Ali: What is her excuse? He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: And mothers suckle their children for two whole years. And He said: And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months. So pregnancy is six months, and weaning is twenty-four months. He said: So Umar let her go. He said: Then she gave birth thereafter after six months. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man married a woman and consummated with her on the night he married her, then she produced with him a complete child after six months — is she stoned? Then he mentioned Ali and what he said concerning that."
"13072","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: A woman who gave birth after six months was raised to Uthman, and he said: A woman was raised to me, I do not see him except that he said: And she has come with evil, or the like of this — she gave birth after six months. Ibn Abbas said to him: When she completes suckling, pregnancy is six months. He said: And Ibn Abbas recited: And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months. So when she completes suckling, pregnancy is six months."
"13073","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from a guide of Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with him when a woman who had given birth after six months was brought to Uthman, and Uthman ordered her stoning. Ibn Abbas said to him: If she disputes with you by the Book of Allah, she will defeat you. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months. So pregnancy is six months and suckling is two years. He said: So it was averted from her. From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Ikrimah, and more than one mentioned that Umar was brought the like of what Uthman was brought, and Ali said concerning it the like of what Ibn Abbas said."
"13074","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me, that Nafi' ibn Jubayr informed him, that Ibn Abbas informed him, he said: I am indeed the companion of the woman who was brought to Umar and had given birth after six months, and the people disapproved of that. I said to Umar: Why do you wrong? He said: How? He said: I said to him: Recite: And his bearing and his weaning are thirty months. And He said: And mothers suckle their children for two whole years. How much is a hawl? He said: A year. He said: I said: How much is a year? He said: Twelve months. He said: I said: So twenty-four months are two whole hawls, and of pregnancy Allah advances what He wills and delays. So Umar was eased by my saying."
"13075","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, that a woman whose husband died, then a man hinted marriage to her, until when she was alone with her husband, then she remained four months and half a month, then she gave birth. The man said: What is this? She said: He is from you. He said: No, by Allah, he is not from me. Their affair reached Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he sent to the woman and asked her. She said: He is, by Allah, his son. He asked about the woman, and he was told only good about her. Umar was perplexed, then he sent to women of the women of the Jahiliyyah and gathered them, and asked them about her affair and told them her story. A woman among them said to her: Did you menstruate? She said: Yes. She said: I shall tell you the story of this woman. She became pregnant by her first husband, and she used to bleed over it, so her child shrank upon the bleeding, until when she married and the water of her husband reached her, he revived and moved, and the blood ceased from her. So this is when she gave birth at the completion of nine months. The women said: She has spoken the truth; this is its matter. So Umar separated between them, and said: I did not separate between you in anger against you, and I asked about you and nothing but good reached me, but I wanted women to be cautious and not to hasten to marriage. From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Umar, the like of it, and he added: And he attached him to the first."
"13076","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who married a woman, and she turned out pregnant, and he had consummated with her, he said: If she brings him within less than women give birth in, they are separated, and she has the dower."
"13077","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: A man divorced his wife, and she completed the waiting period with three menstruations, then she married a man, then her pregnancy from her first husband became evident. Abd al-Malik separated between them, and gave her dower from her latter husband for what he had of her, and he attached the child to the first, and ordered her to observe the waiting period."
"13078","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from shaykhs of theirs, from Umar, that a woman was raised to him whose husband had been absent from her for two years, then he came and she was pregnant, so Umar was about to stone her. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said to him: O Commander of the Faithful! If you have a way against her, you have no way against what is in her belly. So Umar left her until she gave birth to a boy whose front teeth had grown. Her husband recognized his likeness in him. Umar said: Women are incapable of giving birth to the like of Mu'adh. Had it not been for Mu'adh, Umar would have perished."
"13079","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who had intercourse with a slave girl of his in which there is partnership, he said: He is flogged one hundred, and she and her child are valued against him. Ma'mar said: So I asked Ibn Shubrumah, he said: She is valued against him, and her child is not valued, because he is a child of his father and he is free."
"13080","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Ibn al-Musayyib was asked, and two men with him from the jurists of Medina, about a man who had intercourse with a slave girl of his in which there is partnership, and they said: He is flogged one hundred less a lash, and she and her child are valued against him."
"13081","From Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Sabrah, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Abu al-Zinad informed us, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Each one of them is to be given the lesser hadd, and if it is her child, then the qafah are to be called for him. Ibn Jurayj said it, and Ikrimah ibn Khalid said it also."
"13082","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Asim informed me, concerning a slave girl owned between two men in halves, and both of them had intercourse with her in one purity period, with three nights between them, and she gave birth to a boy. Abd al-Malik wrote to his governor in Medina to ask Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. Ibn al-Musayyib said: Write to him — and he himself refused to write — that they call the qafah, and they attach him by resemblance, and each one of them is to be flogged half the punishment, for stoning was averted from them only by the share of each one of them in her. Then each is to sell his half-share of the boy who was not attached to him to the one to whom he was attached, and he is to be lenient with him concerning it. Abd al-Malik did that."
"13083","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata and Dawud ibn Abi Asim, that a woman died in al-Sham and left a slave girl between her husband and partners, and her husband had intercourse with her, and he owned a fourth of her. Ibn Bahdal, a judge of the people of al-Sham, was approached concerning that and said: Stone him. Then that reached Ibn Ghanam, and he said: Flog him three-fourths of the hadd, and he did not order his stoning because of what he owned in her."
"13084","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a slave girl passed around by merchants, they said: The qafah are called and they attach by resemblance, and his mother remains a slave, and they are made an example of for the like of this."
"13085","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who had intercourse with a slave girl of his in which there is partnership, he said: He is flogged one hundred, and she and her child are valued against him, then he is made to pay the price to his partner. As for Ibn Shubrumah and others of the people of Kufa, they say: She is valued against him, and her child is not valued against him."
"13086","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, concerning the slave girl owned between two men, and she gives birth by one of them, he said: The hadd is averted from him by his ignorance, and he guarantees his partner his share and half the price of his child. He said: And if she belongs to two brothers and one of them has intercourse with her and she gives birth, he said: The hadd is averted from him, and he guarantees his brother the value of his share of the slave girl, and there is no value on him for her child, because he is freed when he owns him."
"13087","From al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu al-Sariyyah, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who had intercourse with a slave girl between him and partners. He said: He is a traitor; there is no hadd on him. Sufyan said: And we say: No flogging and no stoning, but ta'zir."
"13088","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: He is flogged one hundred, whether muhṣan or not muhṣan."
"13089","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: It is not lawful for a man to tread a private part except a private part which, if he wishes he sells, and if he wishes he gifts, and if he wishes he frees."
"13090","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab that a man had intercourse with a slave girl of his in which there is partnership, and had intercourse with her, so Umar flogged him one hundred lashes less a lash."
"13091","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who had intercourse with a slave girl of the spoils before division, he said: He is flogged one hundred less a lash, whether muhṣan or not muhṣan."
"13092","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', that a boy of Umar forced a young slave girl of the khums, so Umar beat him and did not beat her."
"13093","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ismail informed me, that a man hastened and had intercourse with a young slave girl of the khums. He said: I thought she was mine. Ali said: I have a right in her. So he did not flog him and did not apply the hadd to him, because of what he owned in her."
"13094","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Nafi', that a boy of Umar had intercourse with a young slave girl of the khums, forcing her, and had intercourse with her, and he was in charge of those slaves, so he flogged him the hadd and exiled him, and left the girl and did not flog her because he had forced her."
"13095","From Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, that he was a slave of the slaves of the emirate."
"13096","Al-Thawri informed us, from Salih, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Khayr al-Hadrami, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: Ali was in Yemen, and a woman was brought to him with whom three had intercourse in one purity period. He asked two: Do you affirm the child to this one? They did not affirm. Then he asked two: Do you affirm the child to this one? They did not affirm. Then he asked two: Do you affirm the child to this one? Until he finished, asking two about one, and they did not affirm. So he cast lots among them, and imposed the child on the one on whom the lot fell, and imposed on him two-thirds of the diyah. That was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed until his molars appeared."
"13097","Al-Thawri informed us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan, from Ali, he said: Two men who had intercourse with a woman in one purity came to him. He said: The child is for you two, and he belongs to the remaining one of you."
"13098","Abu Hanifah informed us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, concerning two men who have intercourse with a woman in one purity period, then she gives birth, he said: If the first claims him he is attached to him, and if the latter claims him he is attached to him, and if they both doubt concerning him, then he is the son of them both; he inherits them and they inherit him."
"13099","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that two men claimed a child. Umar called the qafah, and followed in that the insight of the qafah, and attached him to one of the two men."
"13100","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Umar and the qafah together saw his resemblance in them both and their resemblance in him. Umar said: He is between you two; you both inherit him and he inherits you. He said: I mentioned that to Ibn al-Musayyib, and he said: Yes, he belongs to the latter of them."
"13101","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: When Umar called the qafah and they saw his resemblance in them both, Umar saw the like of what the qafah saw. He said: I knew that the bitch is impregnated by dogs, each pup belonging to its father. I did not think that two seminal fluids gather in one child."
"13102","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that two men had intercourse with a woman in one purity period, and she became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. The qafah saw his resemblance in them both. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: This is a matter in which I judge nothing. Then he said to the boy: Place yourself where you wish."
"13103","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: A dispute was brought to al-Ash'ari concerning a child claimed by a dihqan and a man of the Arabs. He called the qafah, and they looked at him and said to the Arab: You are more beloved to us than this foreigner, or as he said, but he is not your son, so leave him, for he is his son."
"13104","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who had intercourse with his slave woman in her waiting period from her husband's death, he said: The qafah are called for her child, for Umar ibn al-Khattab and those after him took the view of the qafah in the like of this."
"13105","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: While two women were sleeping, with each one of them her infant, and that was at the first building of Basra, a wolf came and snatched one of the two infants. Each one of them claimed the remaining of the two infants. Their affair was raised to Ka'b ibn Sur, so he called four of the qafah, then called for sand and spread it, then called one of the two parties and ordered them to walk in the sand, then the others walked. Then he brought the infant and placed his foot in the sand, then he separated the qafah and called them one by one and asked them. Each one of them attributed him to one of the two parties, saying: This is his cousin, and this is such-and-such of him, until they all agreed on that. Then he gathered them and said: Do you testify that he is of them? They said: Yes. He said: Four of the Muslims testified; I find no judgment for you other than this. I am not Sulayman ibn Dawud."
"13106","From al-Thawri, concerning two women claiming a child: He belongs to them both together, like men claiming a child."
"13107","From Ibn Uyaynah and others, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While two women were sleeping, with them their two children, a wolf attacked them and took the child of one of them. They disputed to Dawud concerning the remaining, and he judged with him for the elder of them. They went out and Sulayman ibn Dawud met them and said: What did the king judge between you? The younger said: He judged with him for the elder. Sulayman said: Bring the knife; we shall split him between you. The younger said: He belongs to the elder; leave him to her. Sulayman said: He is yours; take him — meaning the younger — when he saw her mercy for him. Abu Hurayrah said: I never heard of the knife at all except that day from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we used to call it only al-mudyah."
"13108","From Ibn Jurayj, concerning the one who does the deed of the people of Lut, he said: He is stoned if muhṣan, and flogged and exiled if unmarried. Ibn Uyaynah said it, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid."
"13109","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: He is stoned if muhṣan, and flogged if unmarried, and severity is added upon him in imprisonment and exile."
"13110","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: He is stoned if muhṣan, and if unmarried he is flogged one hundred."
"13111","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Concerning the man who does the deed of the people of Lut, the hadd of zina: if muhṣan he is stoned, otherwise he is flogged."
"13112","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, raising it to Ali, that he stoned in sodomy."
"13113","From Ibn Jurayj and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that he said: Concerning it is the like of the hadd of the adulterer: if muhṣan he is stoned. From Ibn Abi Sabrah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Amr ibn Sulaym and Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Ibn al-Musayyib, the like of it."
"13114","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, hearing Mujahid and Ibn Jubayr narrating, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Concerning the unmarried found upon sodomy, he said: He is stoned."
"13115","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the doer and the one done to — meaning the one who does the deed of the people of Lut. And whoever comes an animal, kill him and kill the animal. Ibn Abbas said: Lest its people be taunted with it. And whoever comes one of inviolable kin, kill him."
"13116","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that she saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieved, and said: O Messenger of Allah! What grieves you? He said: Something I feared for my ummah, that they will do after me the deed of the people of Lut."
"13117","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata al-Khurasani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed seven persons; he cursed one of them with three curses, and cursed the rest each with one curse. He said: Cursed, cursed, cursed is whoever does the deed of the people of Lut. Cursed is whoever reviles any of his parents. Cursed is whoever changes any of the landmarks of the earth. Cursed is whoever joins between a woman and her daughter. Cursed is whoever allies with a people without their permission. Cursed is whoever has intercourse with an animal. Cursed is whoever slaughters for other than Allah, mighty and majestic. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it, except that he did not mention the animal."
"13118","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I asked Ata about the one who comes an animal: Allah was not forgetful to send down concerning it, but it is foul, so deem foul what was foul."
"13119","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Abu Razin, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the one who has intercourse with an animal, he said: There is no hadd on him."
"13120","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning the one who comes an animal, he said: He is flogged one hundred, whether muhṣan or not muhṣan."
"13121","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that Ibn Munabbih informed him: In the Torah, whoever has intercourse with an animal is cursed with Allah."
"13122","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Concerning the man who has intercourse with an animal of the cattle, he said: I have not heard a sunnah concerning it, but we see him like the adulterer, whether muhṣan or not muhṣan."
"13123","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I asked him about a man slandered with an animal, or found upon an animal. He said: There is no hadd on him."
"13124","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Whoever slanders a man with an animal is flogged the hadd of slander."
"13125","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: And let not pity for them take you in the religion of Allah. He said: That is in neglecting the hudud of Allah and not carrying them out. Mujahid said it."
"13126","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning His saying: And let not pity take you for them. He said: That the hadd not be carried out. And concerning His saying: A party of the believers. He said: A party is one man and above."
"13127","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: And let a party of the believers witness their punishment. He said: One to a thousand. He said: And Ata said: Two and above."
"13128","From Ma'mar, from al-Kalbi, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: And let not pity for them take you. He said: Suspending the hudud."
"13129","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Qasim, from his father, that Ali beat a man in a hadd while sitting."
"13130","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: The flogging of the adulterer is severer than the flogging of slander and wine. He said: The flogging of slander and wine is about one. As for wine, they used to strike with hands until Umar made it the hadd."
"13131","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, from al-Hasan, he said: Zina is severer than the hadd of qadhf, and qadhf is severer than drinking."
"13132","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I testify upon my father that he informed me, that his mother ordered a sheep and it was skinned when Umar flogged Abu Bakrah, and she clothed him with it. Was that except from severe flogging?"
"13133","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: As for slander, he is flogged, and he does not raise his hand."
"13134","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Exertion is made in the hadd of zina, and lightness in slander and drink."
"13135","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Exertion is made in the flogging of zina and slander, and lightness in drink."
"13136","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan sent al-Hamdani to carry out the hadd upon Ayyub al-Hamdani and upon Safwan ibn Safwan, with a new whip never flogged with. He said: Raise your hand until when your armpit is seen, that suffices you. He said: I looked at the back of Safwan after he was hadd-punished, and it was not cut open, and I looked at the back of Ayyub and part of it was cut open. He said: And I saw al-Hamdani put their cloaks down when he flogged them."
"13137","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a hadd, so carry it out on me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a whip, and a new whip with its fruit upon it was brought. He said: No, a whip lesser than this. A whip with broken end was brought. He said: No, a whip above this. A whip between the two whips was brought, and he ordered with it and he was flogged. Then he ascended the minbar, and anger was known in his face, and said: O people, Allah the Exalted has forbidden you indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. Whoever incurs any of them, let him veil with the veil of Allah, for whoever raises any of that to us, we shall exact it."
"13138","From al-Thawri, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: A man in a hadd was brought to Umar, and he ordered a whip, and a whip with harshness in it was brought. He said: I want softer than this. A whip with softness in it was brought. He said: I want harsher than this. He said: A whip between the two whips was brought. He said: Strike with it, and let not your armpit be seen, and give every limb its due."
"13139","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, he said: A man in a hadd came to Ali, and he said: Strike, and give every limb its due, and avoid his face and his private parts."
"13140","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from an informant who narrated to him from Ali, he said: A man who drank wine came, and Ali said: Strike, and leave his hands to shield with them."
"13141","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Taymi, from Abu Majid al-Hanafi, that Ibn Mas'ud was brought a man with his brother's son, and he was drunk. He said: I found this drunk, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Shake him, agitate him, and smell his mouth. So they shook him, agitated him, and smelled him, and found from him the smell of drink. Abdullah ordered him to prison, then brought him out the next day, then ordered a whip, and its fruit was pounded until it became a light whip — meaning it turned. He said: Then he said to the flogger: Strike, and draw back your hand, and give every limb its due. He said: Abdullah struck him a beating not severe, yet painful. He said: I said: O Abu Majid, what is severe? He said: The blow of the sharp. He said: What is his saying: Draw back your hand? He said: He does not stretch — meaning he does not extend — and his armpit is not seen. He said: He stood him in a qaba and trousers. He said: Then he said: Evil, by Allah, is the guardian of the orphan, this one. You neither disciplined well, nor covered the ruined one — the ruined one. He said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! He is my brother's son, and I find for him of anguish — meaning compassion — what I find for my child, but I did not spare him. Abdullah said: Allah is Pardoning, He loves pardon, and it is not fitting for a ruler to be brought a hadd except that he carries it out. Then Abdullah began narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: The first man cut among the Muslims was a man of the Ansar, or among the Ansar. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was as if ashes were strewn in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — meaning ashes scattered upon him. They said: O Messenger of Allah! As if this grieved you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents me, while you are helpers of Satan against your brother? Allah is Pardoning, He loves pardon, and it is not fitting for a ruler to be brought a hadd except that he carries it out. Then he recited: And let them pardon and overlook."
"13142","From Israil, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, he said: I witnessed Amir forbidding striking the head of a man slandered while he was being beaten."
"13143","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubayd Allah informed me, that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to choose a man for the hudud, and that Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah used to carry out the hudud, and the governor of Mecca that day was Muhriz ibn Harithah. Then he said to Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah: When you want to flog, do not flog until you pound the fruit of the whip between two stones until you soften it."
"13144","From al-Thawri, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Stripping is not lawful in this ummah, nor stretching, nor fettering, nor shackling."
"13145","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ali, that a man in a hadd was brought to him, and he beat him with a Qastallani cloak on him, sitting."
"13146","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Sirin, he said: I saw Amir al-Sha'bi flog a man in a hadd of slander, and he flogged him with his shirt on him."
"13147","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, he said: I saw Amir al-Sha'bi beat a man who slandered a man, in a shirt, and he did not beat him in the mosque."
"13148","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I asked al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah about the slanderer: Are his clothes removed from him? He said: Nothing is removed from him except a fur or a stuffed garment."
"13149","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, he said: Nothing is put aside from the slanderer except the cloak. Al-Hakam said: Yahya al-Jazzar informed me, from Ali, the like of the saying of Ibrahim."
"13150","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: The slanderer and the drinker are flogged with their clothes on them, and the clothes are removed from the adulterer until he is in his waist-wrapper."
"13151","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Imran ibn Musa informed us, he said: I attended Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz flogging in the hadd. He puts aside the cloak if a shirt is on him, and if an waist-wrapper and cloak are on him, then he puts aside the cloak in every case. He said: As for the shirt, it was sometimes put aside from the man while he was looking and he did not forbid it, and sometimes they wanted to put it aside from the man and he forbade them. He said: As for the cloak, he puts it aside from this and this. He said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad put aside the cloak of Abu al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Hubaysh, with a shirt on him, when they hadd-punished him, and he hadd-punished him before the people."
"13152","From al-Thawri, from Wasil, from Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, he said: A shepherdess woman who committed zina was brought to Umar, and Umar said: Woe to the exposed one; her beauty is gone. Go and beat her, and do not tear her skin. Allah made four witnesses a cover; He covered you with it short of your indecencies, so let none of you uncover the cover of Allah. Had He willed He would have made him a truthful man or a liar."
"13153","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali, that a man flogged a slave girl and she bled, and under her clothes was an iron coat which her people had dressed her in, and he exiled her to Basra."
"13154","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Yahya, from Ali, he said: The woman is beaten sitting, and the man standing, in the hadd."
"13155","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Qasim, from his father, that Ali beat a man in the hadd sitting."
"13156","From Ma'mar, he said: It reached me that the woman is beaten sitting, with her clothes on her, in the hadd."
"13157","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard that the woman is beaten sitting."
"13158","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told that Shurayh used to order concerning her that her legs and shanks be tied to her thighs, and she is flogged thus sitting, with her clothes on her."
"13159","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, concerning his slave woman who was hadd-punished in zina, that he hadd-punished her in zina. He said to the flogger, pointing to the legs: And lighten. I said: Then where is His saying: And let not pity for them take you in the religion of Allah? He said: Should he kill her?"
"13160","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered whoever was with him, and each one of them struck two blows with his sandal or his whip, or what was in his hand, and they were then twenty men or near it."
"13161","From Ma'mar, ... from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered, and they struck with hands and with palm stalks. I was among them."
"13162","Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab was asked: How much did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flog in wine? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix a hadd in it. He used to order those present to strike with their hands and their sandals, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Stop. Abu Bakr fixed in it forty lashes, and Umar fixed in it eighty lashes."
"13163","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying: The one who drank wine, they used to beat him with their hands and their sandals and shove him. That was in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and part of the rule of Umar. Then he feared that the man would be killed, so he made it forty lashes. When he saw them not desisting, he made it sixty. When he saw them not desisting, he made it eighty. Then he said: This is the least of the hudud."
"13164","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab consulted the people concerning the flogging of wine, and said: The people have drunk it and dared upon it. Ali said to him: The drunk, when he is drunk he raves, and when he raves he slanders, so make it the hadd of slander. So Umar made it the hadd of slander, eighty."
"13165","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from Umayr ibn Sa'id al-Nakha'i, he said: Ali said: I would not carry out a hadd upon anyone and he dies, and I feel it upon myself, except the drinker of wine. If he died I would pay his blood-money. That is because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not institute it."
"13166","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ja'far, he said: Ali flogged al-Walid ibn Uqbah forty lashes in wine, with a whip of his with two ends."
"13167","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from a man called Abdullah, from al-Hudayn ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Harith, that Ali ordered Abdullah ibn Ja'far and he flogged him, with Uthman counting until he reached forty lashes. Then he said: Stop. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged forty in wine, and Abu Bakr flogged forty, and Umar completed it eighty. Each is a sunnah."
"13168","From al-Thawri, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, beat in wine with two sandals forty."
"13169","From al-Thawri, from Awf or another, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck in wine eighty."
"13170","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab intended to write in the mushaf that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck in wine eighty, and he appointed Dhat Irq for the people of Iraq."
"13171","Ma'mar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him. Then if he drinks, flog him. Then if he drinks, kill him. Ibn al-Munkadir said: That was left afterwards. Ibn al-Nu'ayman was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he flogged him, then he was brought and he flogged him, then he was brought and he flogged him, then he was brought the fourth and he flogged him, and did not add over that."
"13172","Al-Thawri informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Dhakwan, from Mu'awiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the drinker of wine: When he drinks wine, flog him. Then if he drinks, flog him. Then if he drinks, flog him. Then if he drinks the fourth, strike his neck. Al-Thawri said: Our companions narrated to us from al-Zuhri that Ibn al-Nu'man was struck four times, and killing was lifted."
"13173","From Umar ibn Habib, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, strike him. Then if he drinks the second, strike him. Then if he drinks the third, strike him. Then if he drinks the fourth, kill him. He said: A man who had drunk was brought, and he struck him, then the second and he struck him, then the third and he struck him, then the fourth and he struck him. And Allah the Exalted laid down killing."
"13174","Ma'mar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: Ibn al-Nu'ayman was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) many times, more than four, and he flogged him in all that. A man with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, curse him; how much he drinks, and how much he is flogged. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse him, for he loves Allah and His Messenger."
"13175","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, he said: A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he flogged him, then the second, then the third, then the fourth; in all that he flogged him. He did not add over that."
"13176","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He struck a man in wine four times. And Umar struck Abu Mihjan al-Thaqafi in wine eight times."
"13177","Muhammad ibn Rashid informed us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrating, that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen, asked him and said: My people make a drink from corn called al-mizr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Does it intoxicate? He said: Yes. He said: Forbid them from it. He said: Then he returned and asked him. He said: Forbid them from it. Then he asked him the third, and said: I forbade them from it, and they did not stop. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not stop, kill him."
"13178","From al-Thawri, from Ata, from his father, that Ali beat al-Najashi al-Harithi the poet; he drank wine in Ramadan, so he beat him eighty, then imprisoned him. He brought him out the next day and beat him twenty, then said to him: I flogged you these twenty for your daring against Allah and your breaking fast in Ramadan."
"13179","From al-Thawri, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: An old man who had drunk wine in Ramadan was brought to Umar, and he said: For the nostrils, for the nostrils, while our boys are fasting. He said: He beat him eighty, then exiled him to al-Sham."
"13180","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning the slave who drinks wine, he said: He is struck half the hadd of the free. Uthman struck a boy of his half the hadd in wine."
"13181","From Ma'mar and Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that Umar and Uthman and Abdullah ibn Umar flogged their slaves in wine half the hadd of the free."
"13182","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Imran ibn Musa informed me that he attended Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad allowed the testimony of the slanderer after he repented."
"13183","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning His saying: And never accept their testimony. He said: When the slanderer repents, his testimony is accepted."
"13184","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: When he repents from his slander, his testimony is accepted."
"13185","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When the slanderer repents, it is accepted. His repentance is to belie himself."
"13186","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Three testified against al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah with zina, and Ziyad was discredited. Umar hadd-punished the three, and said to them: Repent; your testimony will be accepted. Two men repented, and Abu Bakrah did not repent. His testimony was not accepted. Abu Bakrah was the brother of Ziyad by his mother. When there was of the affair of Ziyad what there was, Abu Bakrah swore never to speak to Ziyad. He did not speak to him until he died."
"13187","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Four testified against al-Mughirah with zina, and Ziyad was discredited. Umar hadd-punished the three, then asked them to repent. Two repented and their testimony was accepted. Abu Bakrah refused to repent, so his testimony was not allowed. He had become like an arrowhead from worship, until he died."
"13188","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: Abu Bakrah and Nafi' and Shibl ibn Ma'bad testified against al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah that they looked at him as they look at the kohl stick in the kohl container. He said: Ziyad came, and Umar said: A man has come who testifies only with the truth. He said: I saw an ugly sitting and panting. He said: Umar flogged them the hadd."
"13189","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, that Umar said when the three testified: al-Mughirah has ruined the four."
"13190","From Ma'mar, from Budayl al-Uqayli, from Abu al-Wadi', he said: Three men testified against a man and a woman with zina, and the fourth said: I saw them in one garment. If this is zina, then that is it. Ali flogged the three, and disciplined the man and the woman."
"13191","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Imran ibn Musa informed me, he said: Hisham ibn Miswar ibn Makhramah and al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf reviled one another before Hisham ibn Ismail, and Hisham ibn al-Miswar slandered al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim. Hisham ibn Ismail seized him. Imran said: I do not say: I attended that of their affair, but I say: It happened. He said: Then I attended Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz in the last of his time, while he was over Medina, and Murrah ibn Abi Murrah and Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah, freedmen of al-Kathir ibn al-Salt, disputing. I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah claim the testimony of Hisham ibn al-Miswar. Murrah said: That is a man whose testimony is not allowed against me nor against a Muslim, because he is hadd-punished, resented. Umar said to him: Is that to you or to your mother? He ordered him, and he was brought near him until the stick reached him. He struck him with it until he split it upon his head and his hands. Then he ordered him and he was dragged on his buttocks until he reached the end of the row. Then he turned to Abdullah ibn Abi Murrah, the claimant of the testimony of Hisham, and said: The testimony of Hisham is allowed for you, along with an upright."
"13192","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Imran ibn Musa informed me, that there was between Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah and Abu al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn al-Saib a dispute. He said: Abu al-Harith slandered Isa before Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, so Abu Bakr hadd-punished Abu al-Harith while I was present. He said: Then I attended Abu Bakr after that, and he judged between two, with Abu al-Harith present. He ordered his scribe to write the testimony of Abu al-Harith upon that judgment of his, and men of Quraysh. Imran said: The slander of Abu al-Harith against Isa was that a woman of them, her father entrusted her property and her marriage to Isa. Her uncle Iyyad ibn Nawfal ibn Abdullah ibn Nawfal married her off, and she is the daughter of the brother of Iyyad ibn Nawfal. Isa spoke to Umar concerning that, and he annulled her marriage. Then Isa proposed to her to herself, and she agreed. Isa mentioned that to Umar, and he sent Ibn al-Munkadir and another, and they mentioned that to her, and she was silent. Isa married her. When Abu al-Harith and Isa disputed to Abu Bakr, Abu al-Harith said: And this one, you approach the wife of a Muslim man. Abu Bakr wrote concerning that to Umar while he was caliph, and he wrote: Hadd-punish Abu al-Harith."
"13193","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger judged that the testimony of three, nor two, nor one is not accepted for zina, and they are flogged eighty eighty, and their testimony is not accepted until sincere repentance and reform become clear of them to the Muslims."
"13194","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and others, he said: The testimony of the slanderer is never accepted; his repentance is only between him and Allah. He said: Shurayh said it also."
"13195","From al-Thawri, from Wasil, from Ibrahim: The testimony of the slanderer is not accepted; his repentance is between him and his Lord, mighty and majestic. Al-Thawri said: And we are upon that."
"13196","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, who said: A man came to him and testified before him, so he said: Get up, we know you, and he had been flogged with a hadd for qadhf."
"13197","From al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Shabi, from Shurayh, who said: I accept the testimony of every person liable to a hadd except the slanderer; his repentance is between him and his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"13198","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, from al-Shabi, who said: I heard him saying: Allah accepts his repentance, but you do not accept his testimony, meaning the slanderer. He said: And I hold this view."
"13199","From Mamar, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, who said: Four men testified against a man for zina before Muhammad ibn Zayd, who was a judge in Khurasan; they were not proven upright, so stoning was averted from the man, and he left the witnesses and did not apply the hadd to them. He said: And I do not consider it a hadith; their testimony was not valid in his view since they were not proven upright."
"13200","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: Two men testified, We saw him on top of her, adding nothing more. He said: They are punished as a deterrent."
"13201","From al-Thawri, concerning people who testified against a man and a woman, We saw him on top of her, adding nothing more. He said: The man and the woman are given tazir, but the witnesses are not given tazir."
"13202","Ibn Jurayj reported: I was present when Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah flogged a man with the hadd for slander; when he finished, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabia mentioned to him that it is part of the established practice that he be asked to repent at that point, so Abd al-Aziz said to the flogged man: Repent. And I thought he said: I repent to Allah."
"13203","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: One of the scholars of Medina informed me that they all agree that everyone who commits the act of the people of Lut, or commits zina, or slanders, or drinks, or steals, or commits brigandage is asked to repent."
"13204","From Ibn Jurayj, and Abu Bakr reported from more than one person, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: The sunna of the hadd is that its recipient is asked to repent when the flogging is finished. Ibn al-Musayyab said: If he says, I have repented, while he is displeased, his testimony is not accepted."
"13205","From Ibn Jurayj, and al-Thawri, from Ibn Khusayfa, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, who said: A man who had stolen a shawl was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this man has stolen? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not think he steals. Did you steal? He said: Yes. He said: Take him away and cut off his hand, then cauterize it, then bring him to me. So they brought him, and he said: Repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: I repent to Allah. He said: O Allah, accept his repentance. From Mamar, from Ayyub, the like of it."
"13206","From Mamar, from Ibn al-Munkadir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off a man, then ordered him to be cauterized, and said: Repent to Allah. He said: I repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the thief has his hand cut off, it falls into the Fire; if he returns to theft it follows it, and if he repents he recovers it. Abd Allah says, meaning: he takes it back."
"13207","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, that he disliked masturbation. I said: Is there anything due for it? He said: I never heard of anything."
"13208","From al-Thawri, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about it, and he said: That is one who marries himself."
"13209","From al-Thawri and Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abi Razin, from Abi Yahya, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man said: I play with my penis until I ejaculate? He said: Marrying a slave woman is better than it, and it is better than zina. From Mamar, from al-Amash, the like of it with its chain, from Ibn Abbas."
"13210","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Muslim, who said: I saw Said ibn Jubayr meet Abu Yahya, and they discussed the hadith of Ibn Abbas; Abu Yahya said to him: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who plays with his penis until he ejaculates? Ibn Abbas said: Marrying a slave woman is better than this, and this is better than zina."
"13211","From al-Thawri, from Abbad, from Mansur, from Jabir ibn Zayd, Abu al-Shatha, who said: It is your fluid, so emit it."
"13212","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr informed me, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: It is nothing but that one of you rubs his penis until he emits fluid."
"13213","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr informed me, from Mujahid, who said: Those who came before used to command their youths to masturbate, and likewise the woman inserts something. We said to Abd al-Razzaq: What does she inserts something mean? He said: He means al-saqq; he says: she suffices herself with it against zina."
"13214","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Dinar said: I see no harm in masturbation."
"13215","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Concerning a slave woman who committed zina while owned, and the hadd was not applied to her until she was freed, he said: The hadd of a slave woman is applied to her, because it became due upon her while she was owned. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, the like of it."
"13216","From Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, who said: Said al-Maqburi informed me that he heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the slave woman of one of you commits zina, let him flog her and not rebuke her nor scold her; then if she commits zina let him flog her and not rebuke her nor scold her; then if she commits zina a third time, let him sell her, even for a rope of hair."
"13217","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayra and from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the slave woman who was never married? He said: If she commits zina, flog her; then if she commits zina, flog her; then if she commits zina, flog her; then if she commits zina a third or fourth time, al-Zuhri doubts, then sell her even for a dafir."
"13218","From Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayra, who says: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the slave woman of one of you commits zina and her zina becomes evident, let him flog her the hadd and not blame her; then if she commits zina and her zina becomes evident, let him flog her the hadd and not blame her; then if she commits zina a third time, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."
"13219","Muhammad ibn Rashid reported that he heard Makhul saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the slave woman commits zina, flog her; then if she commits zina a third time, sell her even for a dafir."
"13220","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Ala, from Maysara al-Tuhawi Abu Jamila, from Ali, who said: A slave girl of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, committed zina, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Ali to flog her; Ali found her having given birth, so he did not flog her until she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, then he flogged her fifty lashes, and he said: You did well."
"13221","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Hasan ibn Muhammad informed him that Fatima, daughter of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, flogged a slave woman of hers. From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan, the like of it."
"13222","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Maqil ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani came to Abd Allah and said: A slave girl of mine committed zina? He said: Flog her fifty. He said: She has no husband. He said: Her Islam is her chastity."
"13223","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya, from Ibrahim, who said: Alqama and al-Aswad used to apply the hudud upon the slave girls of their people."
"13224","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: The sunna has passed that the slave and slave woman are punished for immorality by their households, unless their matter is raised to the ruler; and no one may preempt the ruler. From al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, the like of it."
"13225","From Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Abd Allah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia said: Some slave girls of the administration committed offenses, so Umar ibn al-Khattab ordered young men from the youth of Quraysh, and they flogged them the hadd. He said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash said: And I was among those who flogged them."
"13226","From Ibn Uyayna, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia informed me, saying: Some slave girls of the administration committed offenses, so Umar ibn al-Khattab sent youths of Quraysh, and they flogged them the hadd. He said: And I was among those who flogged them."
"13227","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: Concerning the slave woman who has no husband, if she commits zina she is flogged half of what is upon the chaste women of punishment; her master flogs her, and if she is married her matter is raised to the ruler."
"13228","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that Umar ibn al-Khattab flogged virgin slave girls from the khumus for zina."
"13229","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata and Amr, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah, from his father Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabia, that he asked Umar ibn al-Khattab about the hadd of the slave woman? He said: She has cast her fur behind the house."
"13230","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabia, that he asked Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab about the hadd of the slave woman, and he said: She has cast her fur behind the house."
"13231","From al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ikrima ibn Khalid, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah, from his father, that he asked Umar about the hadd of the slave woman, and he said: She has cast her fur behind the house."
"13232","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to hold there is no hadd upon a slave, nor upon the people of dhimma, the Jews and Christians. From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"13233","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no hadd upon a slave, nor upon a covenanted person."
"13234","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: He used to hold there is no hadd upon a slave, except that the slave woman becomes chaste through marriage, so half the punishment falls upon her; and that was his view."
"13235","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no hadd upon the slave woman until she becomes chaste."
"13236","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, that he used to hold there is no hadd upon the slave, except that a free man marries the slave woman and makes her chaste, so her dower becomes due upon him and she is flogged."
"13237","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A slave committed zina and was not chaste? He said: He is flogged without hadd. He said: I said: And if she commits zina, and no free man made her chaste by marriage? He said: The Book of Allah: When they become chaste."
"13238","From a man, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, concerning the slave woman who commits zina? He said: She is flogged fifty; and if her master pardons her, that is dearer to me. Abd al-Razzaq said: How good it is! We said to him: And do you hold it? He said: Yes."
"13239","From a man, from Salim ibn Miskin, who said: Habib ibn Abi Fadala informed me that Salih ibn Kiriz reported to him that he brought a slave girl who had committed zina to al-Hakam ibn Ayyub. He said: While I was sitting, Anas ibn Malik came and sat, and said: O Salih, what is this slave girl with you? He said: I said: A slave girl of mine committed immorality, and I wanted to hand her to the ruler to apply the hadd upon her. He said: Do not do it; return your slave girl, fear Allah and conceal her. He said: I will not do it until I hand her over. Anas said to him: Do not do it, and obey me. Salih said: He kept pressing me until I said to him: I will return her on condition that whatever sin I bear in it, you guarantee? Anas said: Yes. He said: So he returned her."
"13240","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: A married woman went to a village, was taken in marriage and had intercourse. He said: If she pleads that she was told he divorced her or died, she is not stoned; and if she offers no excuse, she is stoned. I said: And the dower the other man gave her? He said: It belongs to her husband, not her heir."
"13241","Ibn Jurayj said: Amr ibn Dinar said to me: It belongs to all her heirs. He said: I said to Ata: How can she have a dower, when she is a fornicatress who came to him willingly? He said: He did give her a dower, and she took from him for what he got from her."
"13242","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: One of the people of Kufa informed me that Ali stoned a woman likewise: she had a husband, then came to a land and married, without pleading that her husbands death or divorce had reached her."
"13243","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: If she marries while she has a husband, she is flogged one hundred, returned to her first husband, and keeps her dower from her other husband."
"13244","From Mamar, from a man, from Ikrima, who said: She is flogged one hundred and not stoned; she did it openly and proclaimed it."
"13245","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who married a woman in a land, then her first husband came, and she said: He had divorced me. He said: If she does not produce evidence, she is flogged the lighter of the two hadds, separated from her other husband, keeps her dower for what was made lawful of her, is given tazir, returned to her first husband, and he is made to swear by Allah that he had not divorced her; but if she does not claim he divorced her and offers no excuse, she is stoned."
"13246","From al-Thawri, concerning the woman who deceives the man while she has a husband? He said: She is given tazir, and there is no hadd."
"13247","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning the man who marries a fifth wife? He said: He is flogged; but if he divorces one or two of his four wives, then marries a fifth before the waiting period of the divorced one ends, he is flogged one hundred."
"13248","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab said, concerning a man who marries a fifth wife and consummates with her: If he knew that a fifth is not lawful for him, he is stoned; and if he was ignorant, he is flogged the lighter of the two hadds, and she keeps her dower for what he made lawful of her, then they are separated and never join again. And he mentioned the like of this account regarding her knowledge and ignorance: if she was chaste she is stoned and flogged one hundred, and if she was not chaste and did not enter with knowledge that he had four wives, there is no punishment upon her; and if she bears a child, neither she nor her child has inheritance from him."
"13249","From Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, concerning one who deliberately marries a fifth before the waiting period of the fourth of his wives ends, he said: He is flogged one hundred, and not exiled."
"13250","From al-Thawri, concerning the man who marries a fifth, he said: He is given tazir and there is no hadd. Abd al-Razzaq said: And the people hold this."
"13251","Ibn Jurayj reported: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Ali, that when he found a man and a woman in one garment, he flogged each of them one hundred."
"13252","From Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from al-Hasan, that a man found with his wife a man with the door locked upon them and the curtains let down upon them, so Umar ibn al-Khattab flogged each of them one hundred."
"13253","From Budayl al-Uqayli, from Abi al-Wadi, who said: Three men testified against a man and a woman for zina, and the fourth said: I saw them in one garment; if this is zina then it is that. So Ali flogged the three, and gave tazir to the man and the woman."
"13254","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, who said: I heard Makhul reporting that a man was found in a mans house after nightfall wrapped in a mat, so Umar ibn al-Khattab struck him one hundred."
"13255","From Ibn Uyayna, from al-Amash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, who said: Ibn Masud was brought a man found with a woman in a blanket, so he struck each of them forty lashes and displayed them before the people; the womans family and the mans family went and complained of that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, so Umar said to Ibn Masud: What do these say? He said: I did that. He said: Did you see that? He said: Yes. He said: What an excellent view. They said: We came to him seeking justice, and he questions him."
"13256","From al-Thawri and Mamar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Ibn Masud said: Avert the hudud and killing from the servants of Allah as much as you can."
"13257","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Avert the hudud as much as you can."
"13258","From Mamar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that a governor of Umar, Mamar said: and I heard someone other than Amr claiming that Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah wrote to Umar that a man whose slave confessed to zina, so he wrote to him to ask him: Did he know it is unlawful? If he says yes, apply Allahs hadd upon him; and if he says no, inform him it is unlawful, and if he returns apply the hadd to him."
"13259","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Zina was mentioned in Syria, so a man said: I committed zina. It was said: What are you saying? He said: Did Allah forbid it? He said: I did not know Allah forbade it. So it was written to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he wrote: If he knew Allah forbade it, apply the hadd to him; and if he did not know, teach him, and if he returns apply the hadd to him."
"13260","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Hisham ibn Urwa informed me, from his father, that Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib reported to him, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib died, and freed those of his slaves who prayed and fasted; he had a Nubian woman who had prayed and fasted, a non-Arab who did not understand, and suddenly her pregnancy appeared, and she was previously married. He went to Umar in alarm and told him, and Umar said to him: You are the man who brings no good. That alarmed him, so he sent to her and asked her, saying: Are you pregnant? She said: Yes, from Marghush for two dirhams, and she proclaims it without concealing it. He found Ali, Uthman and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf with him, and said: Advise me. Uthman was sitting, then reclined. Ali and Abd al-Rahman said: The hadd has fallen upon her. He said: Advise me, O Uthman. He said: Your two brothers have advised you. He said: Advise me yourself. Uthman said: I see her proclaiming it as if she does not know it, and the hadd is only upon one who knows it. So he ordered her flogged one hundred, then exiled her, then said: He spoke truth; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the hadd is only upon one who knows it."
"13261","From Mamar, who said: Hisham informed me, from his father, that Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib came to Umar with a black slave woman belonging to Hatib, and said to Umar: The emancipation has reached this one, and she has committed immorality, and she was chaste. Umar said to him: You are the man who brings no good. Umar called her and asked her about it, and she said: Yes, from Marghush for two dirhams, and others said from Marghush, while she mentions it without seeing harm in it. Umar said to Ali, Abd al-Rahman and Uthman, while they were sitting with him: Advise me. Ali and Abd al-Rahman said: We hold she be stoned. Umar said to Uthman: Advise me. He said: Your two brothers have advised you. He said: I adjure you to advise me with your own view. He said: I hold the hadd is only upon one who knows it, and I see her proclaiming it as if she sees no harm in it. Umar said: You spoke truth; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the hadd is only upon one who knows it. So Umar struck her one hundred and exiled her a year."
"13262","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar informed me that in a letter of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote: There is no retaliation, no qisas, no wounds, no killing, no hadd, and no exemplary punishment upon one who has not reached puberty, until he knows what is his in Islam and what is upon him."
"13263","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, from Yahya ibn Hatib, from his father, who said: A freedwoman of his called Markush committed zina, and she came proclaiming zina. He asked Umar about her, along with Ali and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and they said: The hadd is applied to her. He asked Uthman about her, and he said: I see her proclaiming it as if she does not know, and the hadd is only upon one who knows it. Umar agreed, so he struck her and did not stone her."
"13264","From al-Thawri, from Mughira, from al-Haytham ibn Badr, from Harqus, who said: A woman came to Ali and said: My husband committed zina with my slave girl? He said: She spoke truth, and she is not lawful to me. He said: Go and do not return, as if he averted it from him due to ignorance."
"13265","From Mamar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, that a caravan from the people of Yemen alighted at al-Harra, with them a woman who had committed immorality; they departed and left her, so Umar was told her story and asked her. She said: I was a poor woman whom no one showed kindness to with anything, so I found nothing but myself. He said: So he sent to her caravan, they were returned, and he asked them about her need, and they confirmed her. So he flogged her one hundred, gave her, clothed her, and ordered them to carry her with them."
"13266","Ibn Jurayj reported: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to me, from his father, that he reported that a woman from the people of Yemen came in a caravan of pilgrims, and they alighted at al-Harra until, when they departed, they left her; a man from them came to Umar and told him that a woman from them had committed zina at al-Harra. Umar sent to her and asked her, and she said: O Commander of the Faithful, I was an orphan with nothing of the world ... upon the masters, and none of them looked after me, and I found nothing but myself, and she was previously married. So he sent after the caravan and returned them, asked them about what she said ... and they confirmed her. So he flogged her one hundred, then clothed her and carried her, then said: Take her away. From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata reporting the like of this, except that he said: They left her at part of al-Harra until she offered herself, so Umar returned her to Yemen and said: Do not mention what she did."
"13267","Ibn Jurayj reported: Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Sufyan narrated to me, from Abi Salama ibn Sufyan, that a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I came driving sheep, and a man met me and scooped for me a handful of dates, then scooped for me a handful of dates, then scooped for me a handful of dates, then overpowered me. Umar said: What did you say? She repeated, so Umar said, gesturing with his hand: A dower, a dower, gesturing with his hand each time he said it. Then he left her."
"13268","From Ibn Uyayna, from al-Walid ibn Abd Allah, from Abi al-Tufayl, that a woman suffered hunger and came to a shepherd asking him for food, but he refused her until she gave herself to him. She said: So he scooped for me three scoops of dates, and she mentioned she was exhausted by hunger. She told Umar, so he said Allahu Akbar and said: A dower, a dower, a dower; every handful is a dower, and he averted the hadd from her."
"13269","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was brought a woman whom a shepherd met in a desert land while she was thirsty; she asked him for water, but he refused to give her water unless she let him fall upon her. She implored him by Allah, but he refused; when she reached exhaustion she enabled him. So Umar averted the hadd from her due to necessity."
"13270","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: The virgin whose chastity is taken by force? He said: Like the dower of one of her womenfolk. He said: And a dower ... that she cry out, or a trace be found on her. I said: The previously married woman? He said: I never heard anything about her."
"13271","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever forces a virgin woman owes her dower, and the hadd is upon him, and no hadd upon her. Mamar said, and Qatada said the like of that. He said: And the sign of the virgin who is forced is that she cry out. And they said: The previously married woman in that is like the virgin."
"13272","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abd al-Karim informed me: I was told, from Ali and Ibn Masud, and the companions of this report it from this, concerning the virgin whose chastity is taken by force: The virgin gets like the dower of one of her womenfolk, and the previously married woman like the dower of her like."
"13273","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who entered upon a woman and she cried out, while another woman was with her, and he seized her as she cried out and fell upon her. He said: If the man did not know, he is flogged the lighter of the two hadds, because of the womans crying and her saying: I am not your wife; and he is charged her dower. And if he knew, the greater hadd is applied to him if he was chaste."
"13274","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab informed me, concerning a virgin deflowered, like the dower of her womenfolk. He said: Abd al-Malik judged by that."
"13275","From al-Thawri, concerning she who says: My chastity was taken by force, the hadd is averted from her, even if there is pregnancy."
"13276","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, who said: I asked him about the man who forces the slave girl, and he said: When the hadd is applied, the dower is void. From Ibn Shubruma, the like of al-Shabis view."
"13277","From Hushaym, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, who said: Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us that a man forced a woman and deflowered her: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, struck him the hadd and charged him a third of her blood money."
"13278","From al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: It reached Umar that a devout woman became pregnant, so Umar said: I see her standing at night praying, then humbling herself and prostrating, and a deviant from the deviants came to her and overpowered her. She came to him and told him just that, so he let her go."
"13279","From al-Thawri, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Ibrahim, who said: It reached Umar about a woman that she was pregnant, so he ordered her guarded until she delivered; she delivered black water, so Umar said: A touch from Satan."
"13280","From Ibn Uyayna, from Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi, from his father, that Abu Musa wrote to Umar about a woman to whom a man came while she slept, and she said: A man came to me while I slept, and by Allah I did not know until he cast into me like a shooting star of fire. So Umar wrote: A Tihami woman who slept deeply; such can happen. And he ordered the hadd averted from her."
"13281","From Mamar, from Qatada, who said: If the slave woman is forced while previously married, half a tenth of her price; and if she was a virgin, a tenth."
"13282","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, that Ali and Ibn Masud said: Concerning the slave woman when forced: If she was a virgin, a tenth of her price; and if she was previously married, half a tenth of her price."
"13283","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shuba, from al-Hakam and Ibrahim, who said: If the slave deflowers the slave woman, there is no dower upon him. Shuba said, and Mansur informed me, from al-Hasan, who said: The dower is upon him."
"13284","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, and he was asked about two men in one house, each with a slave girl, when one of them came and called his slave girl, but his companions slave girl came, and he fell upon her thinking she was his slave girl. He said: I hold the lighter of the two hadds be applied to him, whether chaste or not, since he did not verify and ask about that; and the slave girl is flogged fifty lashes, since she admitted to him."
"13285","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, and from Abi Abd al-Karim, and Mughira, from Ibrahim, that a slave girl was with a man, and his wife feared he would marry her, so she deflowered her with her finger while women with her held her. It was raised to Ali, so he ordered al-Hasan to judge between them, and he said: I hold she be flogged the hadd for slandering her, and charged the dower for deflowering her. Ali said: It used to be said: If camels knew flour they would grind. He said: And Mughira said, from Ibrahim, al-Hasan said: The dower is upon her, and upon the holders. None said it except al-Mughira."
"13286","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, from Ali, that a man had an orphan girl with him; his wife became jealous of her, called women who held her, and deflowered her with her finger, and said to her husband: She committed zina. He swore he would raise her matter, so the slave girl said: She lied, and told him the story. Her matter was raised to Ali, who said to al-Hasan: Speak concerning her. He said: Rather you, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: You shall speak. He said: She is flogged first for what she committed against her, and upon the women is like the dower of one of her womenfolk, besides the blood money divided among them. Ali said: If camels knew flour they would grind. He said: And camels had not ground then. So Ali judged by that."
"13287","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, who said: If a slave girl deflowers a slave girl with her finger, she is charged her dower like the dower of a woman of her womenfolk, and Abd al-Malik judged by that."
"13288","From al-Thawri, from Humayd al-Araj, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Sayfi, that Umar wrote to Abu Musa al-Ashari: And do not reach with chastisement above twenty lashes."
"13289","From Qays ibn al-Rabi, who said: Abu Husayn narrated to me, from Habib ibn Sahban, I heard Umar saying: The backs of the Muslims are a sanctuary, not lawful to anyone except what a hadd removes. He said: And I saw the whiteness of his armpit while he stood himself."
"13290","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ismail ibn Ayyub informed me, from his father and others, from Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, that he said: Punishment by hudud does not reach."
"13291","Ibn Jurayj reported: Muslim ibn Abi Maryam informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed him, from a man of the Ansar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no punishment above ten lashes, except in a hadd of Allahs hudud."
"13292","Ibn Jurayj reported: A slave girl cried out in a house in Damascus seeking help, and she had shed blood in the house, while the owner of the house fled. Al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman wrote about her to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz during his caliphate, so he wrote: He is suspected in himself, so punish him a painful punishment, but do not reach a hadd, and exile him."
"13293","From Ibrahim ibn Uthman, from Ubayd Allah ibn Rafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no striking above ten strikes, except in Allahs hudud, Mighty and Majestic."
"13294","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata saying: I heard Abu Hurayra saying repeatedly: The eye commits zina, the mouth commits zina, the heart commits zina, the hands commit zina, and the foot commits zina, so he counted them likewise; and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"13295","He said: And he informed me that he heard Abu Hurayra saying: He does not commit zina while he commits zina as a believer, nor steal while he steals as a believer, nor drink wine as a believer while he drinks. He said: I only know he said: And when he withdraws from his sin, faith returns to him."
"13296","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, who said: He does not commit zina as a believer while he commits zina, nor steal as a believer while he steals, nor drink wine as a believer while he drinks. He said: And I only know he used to report it from Ibn Abbas."
"13297","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The fornicator does not commit zina while he commits zina as a believer, nor drink wine while he drinks as a believer, nor steal while he steals as a believer, nor embezzle while he embezzles as a believer, nor plunder a plunder to which people raise their eyes while a believer. Mamar said: And Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father: When he does that, faith departs from him. He says: Faith is like a shade. From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, and Qatada, and from a man, from Ikrima, from Abu Hurayra, and from Abi Harun, from Abi Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it. He said: He does not steal while he steals as a believer. He said: This is a prohibition; he says: While a believer, let him not do: meaning let him not steal, nor commit zina, nor embezzle."
"13298","From Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No thief steals while he steals as a believer, no fornicator commits zina while he commits zina as a believer, no one drinks wine, meaning the hudud, while he drinks it as a believer; and by Him in Whose Hand is Muhammads soul, none of you plunders a valuable plunder to which the believers raise their eyes while he is a believer when he plunders it, nor does any of you embezzle while he embezzles as a believer. He said: Then Abu Hurayra says: Beware, beware."
"13299","Ibn Jurayj reported: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me that he heard Nafi ibn Jubayr saying: He does not commit zina as a believer while he commits zina; when he ceases, faith returns to him, not when he repents of it, but when he turns back from the act. He said: And I thought he mentioned that from Ibn Abbas."
"13300","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayra, I think he said: The fornicator does not commit zina as a believer, nor drink wine as a believer, nor steal while he steals as a believer; and repentance is offered thereafter."
"13301","From al-Thawri, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: He used to offer marriage to his slave, saying: Whoever of you wants marriage I will marry him; for no fornicator commits zina except that Allah removes from him the yoke of Islam; if He wills He returns it to him after, and if He wills He withholds it from him."
"13302","Ibn Jurayj reported, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, that Abu Salih narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The fornicator does not commit zina while he commits zina as a believer, nor does the thief steal while he steals as a believer."
"13303","Ibn Jurayj reported: Maymun ibn Mihran informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas, when a man came to him and said: What do you think of a man who kissed a slave woman? Ibn Abbas said: His mouth committed zina. He said: He bought her after? He said: She is lawful to him. He said: And what is the expiation for what passed? He said: He repents and does not return. From Ibn Muharrir, that he heard Maymun ibn Mihran reporting from Ibn Abbas the like of it."
"13304","From Mamar, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas, saying: I kissed a woman not lawful to me. He said: Your mouth committed zina. He said: And what is upon me for that? He said: Seek Allahs forgiveness."
"13305","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas, saying: I kissed a slave girl. He said: Your mouth committed zina."
"13306","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: A man asked Ibn Abbas, saying: A man kissed anothers slave woman. He said: His mouth committed zina. He said: He buys her and has intercourse with her? He said: If he wishes he may do so. He said: And Jafar ibn Burqan informed me, from Maymun ibn Mihran, that he said to Ibn Abbas: What is his repentance? He said: That he not return."
"13307","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, who said: Nothing among people is more common than zina; it has no odor to be found, nor does it appear so that evidence stands upon it."
"13308","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, who said: Evidence is only upon the denier. And Iyad consulted me about a freedwoman accused, saying: He wanted to send to her to examine her, so I forbade him. So he sent to Abu Sufyan ibn Abd Allah and Abi Salama, and they forbade him that."
"13309","And I heard Abu Hanifa asking about a man who slandered a man, and when he raised him he said: His mother is Jewish or Christian. He said: This one is asked, meaning the evidence, that his mother is a free Muslim woman. Sufyan said about the man who denies a mans lineage, which of them is asked for evidence, when he says: You are not the son of so-and-so. He said: The denied one is asked for evidence that he is the son of so-and-so; if he produces it, the slanderer is struck. Sufyan said: Neither the slanderer nor the slandered is made to swear; and likewise all qadhf: if a man slanders a man, he has no evidence, neither is made to swear."
"13310","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he asked him about the slanderer, and al-Zuhri said: He is made to swear. And Hammad said: He is not made to swear. Mamar said: And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz used to make him swear when there was no evidence. We said to Abd al-Razzaq: Which of them is dearer to you? He said: He is made to swear."
